{
  "raw": {
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8822?c=esu": {
      "title": "Temporary Executive Office Manager",
      "description": "Temporary Executive Office Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temporary Executive Office Manager United States | req8822 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search As the Temporary Executive Office Manager, you will need to skillfully manage the day-to-day operations for the provost to help support a robust academic curriculum. You will be an active member of the Provosts office and will work closely with the provost to complete research centered on diligently completing confidential assignments. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your executive level administrative background and strong working communication skills all while effectively managing departmental funds to maximize student centered initiatives. To be successful in this role, you must possess effective interpersonal skills to connect with various departments, the ability to pivot on multiple tasks to meet deadlines, & excellent analytical skills to break down problems executing choices to best support ESU's strategic plan. Your normal hours will be Monday through Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Temporary Executive Office Manager. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Manage large volume of highly\nconfidential materials and handle sensitive communication and tasks requiring\nfollow up; including but not limited to: faculty renewals, tenure, promotion,\nsabbaticals, etc. Act as a liaison to all\ndepartments within the division of academic affairs, as well as to external\nagencies. Ensure the orderly and\nprofessional conduct of business in the Office of the Provost. Coordinate with deans on various\ntasks such as faculty hiring, reviewing/monitoring ATLAS approvals and\ncompliance with contractual processes (tenure, promotions and annual faculty\nevaluations as well as sabbatical and chair assignments). Oversees workflow of various\nprocessing in office to insure timely receipt of information/materials,\ncompleteness and processing of these documents & forms. Some examples are faculty\ncontracts, sabbatical reports, affiliation agreements, grants, etc. Ensure routine correspondence and\ntravel expense processing. Assist with event planning as well as maintain the\nProvost’s calendar. Provide comprehensive support for\nProvost and Assistant to the Provost. Create, edit and revise\nconfidential documents that are sent on behalf of the Provost. Arrange for Provost’s travel\nincluding creating detailed itineraries, researching and making reservations\nfor airline tickets, rental care, and hotels, and scheduling meetings with all\nappropriate parties. Researches possible agenda items,\nprepares agendas and handouts for weekly and monthly re­ occurring meetings,\nsuch as faculty meetings, Dean's & Director's Meetings, Council of\nTrustees, etc. To interpret for faculty and\nacademic affairs support staff technical and other detailed guidelines,\npolicies and procedures from the Division of Academic Affairs, the University\nand the State System. Coordinates with the Pennsylvania\nState System of Higher Education Offices for routine meetings and\ncorrespondence. Monitor daily communications via\nphone, email and social media accounts and alert Vice President and Assistant\nto the Provost about emerging issues. Responsible for extensive\nconfidential office working files, and inputting/updating information as needed\ninto Academic Affairs databases/spreadsheets on shared network drives. This\nincludes, but is not limited to, personnel files, curriculum approvals, etc. Proficient skill utilizing all\ncomponents of Microsoft Office applications including PowerPoint, Microsoft\nWork, Microsoft Excel/spreadsheets, etc. Also knowledge of the following\napplications is preferred; SAP, Banner, ATLAS, BI- Business/Budget application\nand ability to quickly learn and master new applications e.g. HR acuity. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Related Bachelor's Degree or\nappropriate coursework preferred. Advanced computer software\napplications and skills are required; experience with Windows, word processing,\nspreadsheets and data base systems are essential. Excellent documented verbal and\nwritten communication skills. PowerPoint development or\nequivalent experience preferable. Previous experience as a secretary,\noffice manager, or administrative assistant preferred. Must be able to coordinate and\nwork on multiple projects. Strong interpersonal and listening\nskills, excellent verbal and writing skills, Strong prioritization, analytical,\norganizational and communication skills. Preferred Banner, SAP and BI-\nBusiness/Budget application. Technical skills: Word (tables, reports, merging),\nExcel (formulas, pivot tables, graphs), and MS Teams. Able to think critically and apply\ncritical thinking skills to solve problems independently; make independent\ndecisions that support the needs of the University and its students. Related college course work preferred. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer (If Eligible) Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: Based on Experience Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8821?c=esu": {
      "title": "OASIS Reader/Scribe Student Worker",
      "description": "OASIS Reader/Scribe Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) OASIS Reader/Scribe Student Worker United States | req8821 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search OASIS Reader or Scribe Job Summary: Provide required accommodation\n  for students with documented disabilities. The actual functions of this\n  position will depend on the student with disabilities functional limitations,\n  course requirements and schedule. Reader: A reader is responsible for reading tests to students enrolled in classes. A\n  reader must have a clear speaking voice and with which inflections do not\n  give bias to assessment content. Scribe: A scribe is responsible for\n  providing writing support to eligible students. Qualifications: Currently enrolled student at East Stroudsburg University. Cumulative GPA of 3.0. Excellent and professional communication and interpersonal skills. Ability\n  to interact with a diverse population of students. Strong commitment to assisting students with disabilities. Additional Information: Up to 20 hours per week $7.25 hourly rate Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8820?c=esu": {
      "title": "Museum & Planetarium Tour Guide & Educational Specialist",
      "description": "Museum & Planetarium Tour Guide & Educational Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Museum & Planetarium Tour Guide & Educational Specialist United States | req8820 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Museum & Planetarium Tour Guide & Educational Specialist The Student Worker Tour Guide & Educational Specialist\ndelivers high-impact, hands-on learning experiences for museum and planetarium\nvisitors. Beyond leading gallery tours and planetarium presentations, this role\nfacilitates interactive curriculum-aligned workshops, inquiry-based STEM\nactivities, and specialized educational programs for visiting K–12 schools,\ncampus classes, and community groups. Responsibilities: Interactive Workshop Facilitation: Prepare,\n     lead, and adapt grade-banded, hands-on educational workshops and STEM labs\n     for visiting K–12 classes, camp groups, and scout troops using\n     inquiry-based instructional strategies. Exhibit Tours & Group Instruction: Deliver structured, engaging tours across wildlife, natural history,\n     and space science displays tailored to diverse age brackets and learning\n     needs. Planetarium Presentations: Operate digital\n     planetarium projection equipment and multimedia consoles to run recorded\n     shows and facilitate live night-sky talks. Educational Materials & Activity Prep: Set up, maintain, sanitize, and inventory workshop materials, pop-up\n     carts, discovery boxes, and tactile learning stations. Visitor Services & Floor Safety: Greet groups, manage check-in and admissions procedures, answer\n     visitor questions in person and by phone, and monitor galleries to protect\n     exhibits and ensure collections safety. Program Support & Operations: Assist with\n     facility opening and closing procedures, adhere to uniform and shift\n     coverage protocols, and support special campus-wide events or educator\n     receptions. Qualifications: Currently enrolled undergraduate\n     student eligible for Federal Work-Study. Demonstrated confidence in public speaking and group management,\n      especially with young learners and children. Familiarity with or passion for hands-on, inquiry-based teaching,\n      science communication, and nature exploration. Strong verbal communication, interpersonal agility, and teamwork\n      skills. Technical comfort or willingness to learn planetarium audiovisual\n      systems and multimedia setups. Availability: Consistent availability for\n     weekday morning and afternoon field trip blocks, alongside rotating\n     weekend public hours or special evening functions. Preferred Academic Majors: Elementary Education, Early Childhood Education, Special Education, Middle Level Education, Secondary Education, Science Education or related disciplines. Additional Information: Hourly rate of pay $12.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8772?c=esu": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker 1",
      "description": "Custodial Worker 1 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Custodial Worker 1 United States | req8772 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search As the Custodial Worker 1, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable completing routine custodial care for the University Buildings and surrounding grounds. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Manager of Building Care Services to help achieve consistent building care for ESU. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your custodial and maintenance experience while safely using cleaning products to sanitize the buildings and surrounding area. To be successful in this role, you must be self-motivated, detail-oriented, and have time management skills. Your normal hours will be Friday to Tuesday 8:00 AM to 4:00 PM. You may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Custodial Worker 1. Indoor work is 90% of the role with 10% of the role occasionally completed outside in the snow and or rain. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Sweeps, mops, vacuums, scrubs, waxes, and buffs floors. Cleans, dusts, and polishes furniture and fixtures. Washes and cleans windows, walls, and doors. Cleans toilets, sinks, and mirrors in restrooms and replaces restroom supplies. Utilizes tools and equipment of the custodial trade in the performance of cleaning tasks. Gathers and disposes of waste products, recyclable materials, infectious waste, and hazardous materials according to safe material handling guidelines. Moves furniture and equipment when necessary to perform custodial tasks. Secures and maintains cleaning equipment; requests, picks up, and stores related supplies. Reports needed repairs to crew leader or supervisor. Shovels snow, sweeps and cleans walks, and assists in keeping immediate outside premises and building entrances in an orderly condition. Performs incidental assignments, such as removing ashes, replacing lightbulbs, and making simple repairs. Documents work performed. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Able to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Able to lift, push, pull, or carry 50lbs. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary\n     range: $32,724 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
