    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8796?c=esu": {
      "title": "Mailroom-Warehouse Supervisor",
      "description": "Mailroom-Warehouse Supervisor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Mailroom-Warehouse Supervisor United States | req8796 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search As the Mailroom-Warehouse Supervisor, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable overseeing the day-to-day operations of the ESU Mailroom Receiving and Distribution Center. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Customer Care Manager to provide excellent leadership for your team of two dedicated clerks to accomplish departmental goals. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your complex clerical experience and your strong communication skills all while collaborating with various stakeholders. To be successful in this role, you must be detail oriented, possess the ability to analyze problems and implement efficient solutions, along with effective supervision skills. Your normal schedule will be Monday to Friday 9:00 am to 5:00 pm but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Mailroom-Warehouse Supervisor.  This position will require up to 5% local travel. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Supervise the Mailroom, Receiving\nand Distribution Center staff, associates and student workers. Plan, schedule,\nmonitor and assign routs, shifts and work to varied staff. Assure work is\ncompleted on schedule in\nthe most expeditious and economical means possible to meet identified\ndeadlines, timeframes and the overall campus needs. Coordinate staff to ensure\nthat the staff is fully utilized. Ensures quality customer service is delivered\nand maintained while serving the campus community. Supervisor\nwill perform tasks which includes but are not limited to, receiving, sorting, delivering,\ncollecting and handling of all types of campus mail and packages. Receiving and\ndelivering supplies and equipment to various campus buildings. Operating postal\nand warehouse equipment. Transporting and collecting outgoing and incoming mail\nand packages from the East Stroudsburg United States Postal Service office. Ensures that the storeroom’s\ninventory and data systems are categorized and kept up to date. Works with\nappropriate departments (Business\nOffice and Purchasing Office) as per the State Auditor's requirements to submit\nannual reporting. Identify and rectify inventory discrepancies. Supervise and\nassist with inventory counts and warehouse functions. Ensures the mailroom,\nreceiving and distribution center are in compliance with Federal Postal regulations. Ensures industry standards and regulations are meet relating to storing of\nsupplies, equipment and other materials. Monitor and adhere to cost and policy\nchanges related to postal service fees and services. Perform directory\nupdates and delivery location verification on a regular basis. Prepare and\nupdate reports, manuals, operating procedures, bulk mailing request forms and\nother related documents. Compile and maintain departmental\nbilling, inventory, electronic data records and reports on postal charges -\ni.e. business reply, postage due, inventory, visitor/customer assistance logs,\nand bulk mail. Submit reports and invoices to appropriate departments.\nFollow-up on unpaid charges with the appropriate departments. Schedule\nmaintenance of mailroom and warehouse equipment and vehicles. Handle the\ntransporting of multiple university vehicles to and from maintenance/repair and\nor campus assigned appointments. Coordinate,\ntrack and attend forklift training and certification for the Facilities\nManagement staff. Train staff and student workers to use various equipment,\nsoftware and databases to preform proper mailroom and warehouse operations. Conduct regular and timely performance evaluations of supervised employees. Review, discuss and provide guidance, coaching, direction and/or feedback to staff about job responsibilities and performance. Maintain an active\ndriver's license in order to operate state vehicles on or off campus as directed. Maintain certifications for operation of equipment. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Working knowledge\nof computer software (Microsoft Office Suite: Excel, Access, etc.); and the\nability to perform clerical responsibilities such as typing, organizing office\nfiles, logs, forms, and utilizing scheduling systems. Advance\nability to use computers, video conferencing tools, software applications and\ntools to perform job related responsibilities. Ability to\nunderstand and follow written and oral directives. Ability to multi-task,\nprioritize and manage time effectively High\ndegree of capability in decision-making within the guidelines, written\nprocedures and polices set forth by the university. Ability\nto handle emergency requests with results being accomplished quickly and\ncorrectly. Ability\nto remain professional and courteous with customers at all times. Education & Experience: One year of complex clerical work experience; Completion of a high school business curriculum; or an equivalent combination of experience and/or training related to the responsibility and job duties.  Knowledge of standard office procedures, practices, conduct, and actions. Physical Demands: Exposed to physical conditions such as daily motion activity, frequent lifting (100 pounds maximum), carrying, pushing and pulling, and extensive hand coordination movement is required. Mental Demands: Extended\n  visual attention needed to prepare, compile, and distribute mail and\n  correspondence. Demonstrate a proficiency and knowledge of varied postal and\n  service regulations. Comprehension of written and/or oral communication. Working\nConditions: Individual will operate a\nmotor vehicles and will travel. Additionally, individual will be exposed to the\nseasonal working conditions due to weather variations outdoors. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $41,506 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8792?c=esu": {
      "title": "Academic Secretary",
      "description": "Academic Secretary | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Secretary United States | req8792 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/27/2026 Back to Search As the Academic Secretary, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable serving as the first point of contact for the team delivering excellent customer service to students & their families. You will be an active member of the Nursing & Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences departments and will work closely with the department chairs to coordinate departmental hosted events. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your clerical experience and business background all while completing complex clerical duties to support the day-to-day workflows of the offices. To be successful in this role, you must possess strong pivoting skills, skillfully adapt to a high-volume environment, and have superb task prioritization skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Academic Secretary. You will be coordinating with both department chairs when you are in office for each department. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Perform clerical functions\nincluding but not limited to answering phones, filing, emails, assisting\nwalk-ins, callers, email accepting, and relaying information to appropriate\nmanager and/or supervisor as needed. Perform and process Departmental\nreporting, reporting requests, meeting calendars, recording meeting notes. Help distribute assignments to\nworking students, including scheduling shifts, and reporting hours worked. Coordinate and maintain clinical\nplacements and schedule of students. Assist Clinical faculty and\nClinical Audiologist with scheduling clients in the Speech and Hearing Center. Process documents and perform\nsupport duties for the admission, retention, and graduation of ESU students. Maintain, organize, and purchase\nsupplies and equipment through approved vendors. Assisting Departments Chairs in\nmaintaining and allocating Departmental budgets. Assist Department Chairs on\nDepartmental events. Maintain and organize Departmental\nand student files, documents, and reports. Ongoing training for ClinicNote\nand InPlace platforms. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) High School diploma, associate\ndegree or a combination of experience and education. Minimum of 2 or more years of\nexperience in moderately complex clerical or assistant role, providing support\nservices to a department or an equivalent combination of experience and\ntraining. Two or more years of hands-on\nexperience working with Microsoft Office programs including Teams (chat, calls,\nchannels, etc.), Word (merge, charts, tables), Excel (formulas, pivot tables),\nPowerPoint (animations, voice over), Outlook, and OneDrive. Able to carry out staff\nassignments requiring the organization of material and development of reports\nwith limited supervision. Excellent communication skills are\nrequired to adequately assist students and parents across various platforms\n(i.e., email, face-to-face, phone, Zoom, etc.). Able to prioritize and complete\nmultiple tasks to meet deadlines and write comprehensive correspondence and\nreports. Able to quickly pivot between work\ntasks when unplanned events occur and need immediate attention, as well as\nmanage workload for two departments. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $36,831 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8768?c=esu": {
      "title": "OASIS Secretary",
      "description": "OASIS Secretary | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) OASIS Secretary United States | req8768 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/27/2026 Back to Search As the Secretary for OASIS, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable coordinating the administrative aspects of accommodations for undergraduate and graduate students with disabilities. You will be an active member of the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for Students (OASIS) team and will work closely with the Coordinator to communicate with units to further ESU's commitment and OASIS mission. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your customer service and communication skills while assisting students in connecting with appropriate resources both on and off campus. To be successful in this role, you must be detail-oriented, able to work independently and possess excellent problem-solving skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Secretary for OASIS.  When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Type letters, and memorandums, responsible for purchasing and receiving AT equipment, arranges for webinars, monitor the budget, and other job-related correspondence; maintain and update confidential files. Field inquiries from students and parents needing information about applying for OASIS services including the application process for accommodations, eligibility for services, scheduling intake appointments, the guidelines for documentation, and other questions about OASIS services. Process student requests for accommodation services, create confidential student files, maintain files from initial contacts through completion of the application to the intake appointment, including accepting documentation necessary to determine the eligibility for services. Provide clerical support to the department as directed by the Director and Coordinator of OASIS; create word templates and maintain internal paperwork for students who apply for services requiring completion of applications and supporting documentation. Maintains contact with students requesting services (both intake and continuing services), in person, by phone, or via e-mails, daily. Perform general office duties such as answering the telephone, making appointments, handling mail, disseminating departmental program information, ordering, and maintaining office supplies, keeping calendars up to date, scheduling meetings, and making travel arrangements as needed. Demonstrate a commitment to issues of Social Equity and continue to develop professionally in multi-cultural competence. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Six months as a clerical assistant 1 (commonwealth title), or high school graduate or equivalent combination of experience and training. Able to provide great customer service skills to all students, faculty, and staff. Able to work independently with clear attention to detail. Friendly and professional communication skills. Efficient time management skills and understanding confidentiality. Outstanding communication skills, leading with a student-first attitude. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $36,831 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8814?c=esu": {
      "title": "Residential Advisor 2027-2028",
      "description": "Residential Advisor 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Residential Advisor 2027-2028 United States | req8814 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Resident Advisor Position Description and\nContract 2027-2028 Academic Year Resident Advisor Overview Resident Advisors (RAs) are one tier of our student leadership and community development structure, and they play a vital role in fostering a safe, welcoming, and inclusive living environment in the residence halls. As team members of the Office of Residential Life and Housing, RAs are an integral part of daily Residential Life operations, student support, and community engagement. Resident Advisor Expectations RAs are expected to arrive on time for all scheduled and assigned shifts, including duty nights and training sessions. RAs are expected to remain present and engaged in their community, committing 20–30 hours per week to active (non-sleeping) responsibilities. RAs are expected to find appropriate coverage for duties if they become unavailable, with supervisor approval. RAs are expected to actively participate in all training workshops, in-service programs, and staff meetings. RAs are expected to treat their role as a primary responsibility, second only to academics. RAs are expected to uphold confidentiality, respect individual privacy, and maintain professionalism at all times. Resident Advisor Qualifications RAs must remain full-time undergraduate students in good academic standing by maintaining a minimum overall GPA of 2.5 or higher during employment. RAs must remain in good conduct standing with the University by not being on probationary sanction status or higher during employment. RAs must be at least 18 years old and able to pass all required background checks, including FBI fingerprinting and PA Child Abuse Clearances. RAs must demonstrate strong communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills. Resident Advisor Permitted Hours/Commitment RAs are expected to commit 20 hours per week toward their RA role, including duty coverage, community engagement, administrative tasks, and programming. RAs may hold outside employment or campus involvement as long as it does not interfere with RA responsibilities. Supervisors reserve the right to require RAs to choose between outside commitments and RA duties if performance is impacted. RAs may take up to two weekdays and two weekends off per month, with advance supervisor approval. Resident Advisor Compensation COMPENSATION: Room Waiver plus\nhourly compensation at the established student employment rate, not to exceed\n320 hours per semester, recorded in accordance with the E-Time Processing\nSchedule. Resident Advisor Employee Timelines Fall 2027 RAs will move in as early as Friday, August 6, 2027, by 4:00 p.m. Training begins immediately and continues until the first day of classes. RAs must hold no other commitments during training. RAs assist with Fall 2027 move-in and opening of the halls (specific date\nprovided by Residential Life). RAs provide coverage until Thanksgiving Break when halls close (specific date\nprovided by Residential Life). RAs return for coverage when halls reopen after Thanksgiving Break (specific\ndate provided by Residential Life). RAs provide closing support through the end of Finals Week when the halls\nclose for Winter Break (specific date provided by Residential Life). Spring 2028 RAs move in mid-January (specific date provided by Residential Life). Training begins immediately and continues until the first day of classes. RAs assist with Spring 2028 move-in and opening of the halls. RAs provide coverage through Spring Break (specific date provided by\nResidential Life), when halls close at 7:00 p.m. RAs return for coverage (specific date provided by Residential Life).when\nhalls reopen after Spring Break RAs provide closing support through Spring 2028 move-out until halls close (specific\ndate provided by Residential Life). Note: Dates and times listed are subject to change. Resident Advisor General Responsibilities Build relationships with residents\nand maintain weekly one-on-one engagement. Encourage and support student-initiated programming and community\ndevelopment. Serve as a role model and uphold the Residential Life Core Values and the Way\nof the Warrior tenants. Be available to assist in all openings and closings of assigned residence\nhalls. Provide excellent customer service to residents, families, and guests. Serve in a duty rotation to provide weekday and weekend evening coverage for\nthe residence hall community. Support and attend building and campus-wide events, including open houses and\norientation programs. Enforce and report University policies and procedures, as well as federal,\nstate, and local laws. Respond to emergencies and assist in evacuation drills and crisis situations. Mediate roommate and community conflicts, making referrals to supervisors as\nappropriate. Complete required administrative responsibilities, including weekly\ninteraction logs, duty reports, and bulletin boards. Actively and regularly communicate with supervisors, professional staff, and\nfellow student staff. Respect confidentiality and handle sensitive information appropriately. Participate in hiring, training, and mentoring processes for new staff\nmembers. Support and collaborate with housekeeping, facilities, and University Police\nin maintaining safe and functional living environments. Hourly Rate of Pay: $9.00 to $12.50 based on experience By submitting an application, I\nauthorize the Residential Life and Housing Office to review my student conduct and\nacademic file in relation to my application to the Resident Advisor Position.\nFurther, by signing my name below, I acknowledge that the information contained\nin this application is accurate to the best of my knowledge. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8813?c=esu": {
      "title": "Student Lead Lab Research Assistant Zoology",
      "description": "Student Lead Lab Research Assistant Zoology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student Lead Lab Research Assistant Zoology United States | req8813 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Student Lead Lab Research Assistant Zoology Job Summary: East Stroudsburg University’s Biological Sciences Dept. seeks a student to supports\nacademic research or laboratory operations. Responsibilities include\nassisting with experiments, data collection and analysis, preparing materials,\nand maintaining equipment. They may also be involved in report writing,\ndocumentation, and preparing/presenting presentations. Duties: Safety: A student/lab\nassistant should practice lab safety by following established protocols for\nhandling chemicals, equipment, and biological materials. Assisting with Experiments: This could involve preparing solutions, setting up equipment, and monitoring\nexperiments. Data Collection and Analysis: Collecting data, verifying its accuracy, and potentially analyzing results\nusing various research methodologies. Material Preparation: Preparing\nreagents, media, and other materials needed for experiments and research. Equipment Maintenance: Cleaning\nand maintaining laboratory equipment and ensuring it's in good working\norder. Documentation and Reporting: Recording observations, compiling data, and potentially writing research\nreports. Communication and\nCollaboration: Communicating effectively with researchers and other team\nmembers, potentially including students and instructors. Learning and Development: A\nstudent research/lab assistant is expected to learn new techniques and\nmethodologies under the guidance of their supervisor. Qualifications: East Stroudsburg University’s Biological Sciences Dept. seeks a student who has strong organizational skills, analytical abilities, and effective communication. This student should have experience with basic laboratory techniques and procedures (e.g., lab safety, using equipment, handling samples). Pay Rate: $12.00 Hours per\nWeek: Up to 10 hours per week hours subject to change. Supervisor: Dr. Tracy Whitford Anticipated\nStart Date: September 30, 2026 Anticipated\nEnd Date: May 15, 2028 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8810?c=esu": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Worker-Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) 2026-2027",
      "description": "Graduate Student Worker-Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Graduate Student Worker-Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) 2026-2027 United States | req8810 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate\nStudent Worker with the Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) Department\nworking 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester Pay Rate: $15.00 per hour Responsibilities: Greet students and visitors in a professional and\n     welcoming manner. Assist\n     with front desk coverage as needed. Answer\n     phones and direct calls appropriately. Schedule\n     appointments using the electronic health record and scheduling system. Assist\n     with maintaining confidential records. Assist in\n     planning, coordinating, and implementing mental health outreach programs\n     and campus events. Develop\n     educational materials, social media content, and promotional resources. Represent\n     CAPS at university events, orientations, and resource fairs. Required Qualifications: Enrollment\n     in a graduate program at East Stroudsburg University. Strong\n     organizational and time management skills. Excellent\n     written and verbal communication skills. Ability to\n     maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Proficiency\n     with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and Google Workspace. Ability to\n     work independently and collaboratively. Preferred Qualifications: Enrollment\n     in a graduate program at East Stroudsburg University. Strong\n     organizational and time management skills. Excellent\n     written and verbal communication skills. Ability to\n     maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Proficiency\n     with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and Google Workspace. Ability to\n     work independently and collaboratively. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here:http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8788?c=esu": {
      "title": "Temporary Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Temporary Patrol Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temporary Patrol Officer United States | req8788 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/21/2026 Back to Search As the Temporary Patrol Officer, you will need to be comfortable skillfully assisting the ESU campus through community-oriented policing. You will be an active member of the University Police team and will work closely with the Chief of Police to promote the safety and security of all campus community members. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your law enforcement and interpersonal skills all while interacting with the student population enhancing their ESU experience. To be successful in this role, you must have previous police officer experience, connect professionally with university students to solve issues, along with remaining calm and alert in stressful situations. Your training work schedule will cover 3 shifts: however, upon successful completion of training, your normal hours will be 12:00 AM to 08:00 AM on a 5-week rotation. You may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Temporary Patrol Officer. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Direct and control traffic along with parking on university grounds, enforcing vehicle laws by issuing warnings, parking tickets, citations for violations of university, and commonwealth traffic regulations. Provides safety and Law Enforcement for extra-curricular, social, and recreational events and activities at this university. Practices safety measures to prevent accidents and injuries, and to ensure compliance with applicable regulations. Transport by state-owned vehicles, persons to hospitals and university funds/valuables to proper locations. Investigates suspected crimes, reports findings and arrests where Rules of Criminal Procedure require, following university arrest policy guidelines. Responds to calls, including fire, bomb threat or any other university emergency. Investigates accidents involving persons or property, reporting same and pursuing appropriate course of action on university grounds. Cooperates and works with local, state and other police authorities, as needed. Testifies in court or legal proceedings, as necessary. Utilizes radio communications equipment, accomplishes routine administrative duties and performs other related work as required. Administrative duties include reports, paperwork, incident write-ups, etc. Participates in education and training courses, as requested. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Be 18 years or older and a citizen of the United States. High School Diploma or GED Equivalency. Act 120 certification or active commissioned police officer status.  One year of police experience and formal training in the provisions of basic police services or any equivalent experience or training. The ability to successfully complete the university Firearms Qualification Requirements at required intervals. Must satisfactorily complete Act 180 updates annually. The ability to have & maintain access to the Commonwealth Law Enforcement Assistance Network (CLEAN). Possession and Maintenance of a valid motor vehicle operator's license with the ability to operate state vehicles. Ability to meet such qualifications regarding strength, agility, and health as may be required. Knowledge of commonwealth laws, rules and regulations governing motor vehicle operation and personal conduct for employees or visitors at commonwealth facilities. Knowledge of the hazards and safety precautions appropriate to responsibilities assigned as a law enforcement officer. Knowledge of and skill in practicing emergency first-aid and CPR techniques. Ability to react quickly and calmly in emergency situations and to determine proper courses of action. Ability to enforce laws firmly, tactfully, and with respect for the rights of others. Ability to understand and carry out oral and written instructions. Some knowledge of group behavior. Skill in the use and care of offensive and defensive weapons. Applicant must possess these skills, knowledge, and abilities or be able to explain and demonstrate that they can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some other combination of skills and abilities. Ability to work nights, weekends, overtime and/or any shift. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer If Eligible Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $60,360 annually Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8808?c=esu": {
      "title": "IT Helpdesk Student Worker",
      "description": "IT Helpdesk Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) IT Helpdesk Student Worker United States | req8808 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/18/2026 Back to Search THE ESU IT Helpdesk is Searching for Motivated Students to Join the Team Job Summary: Student will be answering technical questions via telephone, email and walk-ins. Also installing Printer consumable parts; paper, toner and Fuser. Installing software for students and Faculty/Staff to ensure WIFI connections at ESU. Required Skills: Excellent verbal communication skills are essential. Current ESU Student. Students must be reliable and dependable. Student Helpdesk positions are not restricted to Computer Science majors, although students in that major are welcomed. Passing Grade in Personal Computers & their uses (CPSC) is a plus. Duties include: Customer Service for students, staff and faculty via walk-in, email and incoming telephone calls to the helpdesk. Check lab computers and printers for problems. Examples of common tasks include: Assist with file recovery and virus detection on student computers/media. Assist staff with technical tasks; e.g getting laptops setup on ESU. Wireless, re-imaging labs, updating/upgrading software. Assist students in acquiring ESU accounts, resetting passwords. Provide accurate information to students /faculty /parents. Troubleshoot printing issues in the labs. Maintenance of computer lab printers by refilling paper and changing toner. Perform initial routine troubleshooting of computer hardware problems. Additional Information: Students work within the hours of Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 4:00 PM. Hourly rate is $15.00 an hour. Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8807?c=esu": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper Student Helper",
      "description": "Groundskeeper Student Helper | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Groundskeeper Student Helper United States | req8807 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/17/2026 Back to Search Groundskeeper Student Helper Duties: Assist\nwith seed planting, fertilize placement & snow removal with no motorized\nequipment. Assist\nwith general grounds maintenance. Support\nthe planting and care for flowers, grass seed, sod and landscape material. Help staff\nby participating in the watering, fertilizing, sodding, trimming, and cleaning\nof campus lawns and flowerbeds. Help\nmaintain campus regulatory and street signs. Support\nwith cleaning the campus grounds of debris. Help staff\nwith cleaning campus storm and roof drains. Assist\nwith prune campus trees and ornamental plants. Qualifications: Current ESU Student. Ability to lift, push, pull, or carry up to 50 pounds. Additional Information: Work up to 20 hours a week subject hours to change. Hourly Rate $15.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
