    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8802?c=esu": {
      "title": "Clear Path Student Worker",
      "description": "Clear Path Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clear Path Student Worker United States | req8802 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/8/2026 Back to Search Clear Path Chemistry & Biochemistry Student Worker ClearPath\nScholar and Research Program is in need of students majoring in science,\ntechnology and mathematics to aid in the implementation of this NSF Grant\nfunded program. Responsibilities include: Will\nbe expected to travel to the partner community colleges at least once each semester\nto meet with their ClearPath Scholar. Reach\nout in other manners to connect with the student throughout the semester. Once\nthe ClearPath Scholars come to campus, the Mentors will be expected to attend\nClearPath events and meet regularly with the ClearPath scholar. Attend regular\ntraining sessions will occur. Upper-level\nTutors will\nbe expected to establish tutoring times to meet with ClearPath scholars for the purpose\nof tutoring. Required Qualifications to become a Tutor: Current ESU Student. Such students must demonstrate exceptional knowledge in the field in which they are tutoring. All students need to be able to demonstrate targeted skills sets and knowledge requisite for successfully accomplishing the task. Pay Rate & Hours: $10.00 per hour Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
