    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8800?c=esu": {
      "title": "Tutoring Desk Assistant",
      "description": "Tutoring Desk Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tutoring Desk Assistant United States | req8800 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/4/2026 Back to Search The University Wide Tutoring Program is searching for Students to become Desk Assistants Responsibilities include: Actively welcome students and visitors. Ensure students are able to find their tutors. Inform students about tutoring services available for\n      specific courses. Inform students about NetTutor. Maintain a professional and welcoming atmosphere in\n      the tutoring space. Ensure tutors to sign in and out. Ensure the tutoring schedule is current and visible. Keep accurate records of tutor attendance during each\n      shift. Review Groupme for tutors who are running late.\n      Communicate with students that tutor is running late. Review Machform for any absences. Ensure cancellation list is updated and posted at the\n       front desk. Report any tutor absences to the Graduate Assistants\n      (GAs) via email and/or Matthew Simmons. Assist graduate assistants with administrative and\n      promotional tasks and activities as assigned. Organize tutoring tables and chairs (ensuring chairs\n      are pushed in, tables are cleared of debris and cleaned, and supplies are\n      replenished-if necessary). Clean white boards (if your shift ends when tutoring\n      center closes). Take down any dated flyers around the center Foster\nproductivity, accountability, and professionalism during work hours. Required Qualifications to become a Tutor: Current ESU Student Pay Rate & Hours: $10.00 per hour Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
