    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8790?c=esu": {
      "title": "Health & Wellness Peer Educator",
      "description": "Health & Wellness Peer Educator | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Health & Wellness Peer Educator United States | req8790 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/31/2026 Back to Search Health & Wellness Peer Educator Responsibilities: Assistance of maintenance of 6 on-campus Wellness Cabinets. Assistance with delivering donations to the Warrior Food\nPantry at St. Matthews Church. Creating programming to support students, mental, physical, and emotional wellbeing. Coordinate with students for the distribution of\npre-bundled food bags over break periods. Creation of social media posts, pamphlets, posters, and\nother health & wellness media. Promotion at various table events around campus, some of\nwhich may be inside or outside for several hours at a time. Maintain confidentiality of students/staff/community\nmembers who utilize Health & Wellness programming. Attend trainings, workshops, and speaking events as\nprescribed by supervisor. Maintain current knowledge of substance use habits on\ncollege campuses. After training, provide substance-use related education to\npeers in various settings. Required Qualifications: Current ESU student of Public Health, Exercise Science, or related health field. Preferred Qualifications: Interest in Health Education, Preventative Health, and addressing food\ninsecurity/hunger on a college campus. Strong oral and written communication skills. Strong presentation skills focusing on both the ability to\npresent and create presentations (public speaking training and practice can be provided). Ability to handle a variety of tasks and use good time\nmanagement skills. Relatively flexible schedule; able to work evenings\nincluding some weekends, but rarely. Desire to help create a more thriving, healthy campus. A positive attitude that will promote healthy lifestyle choices for yourself and others. Encourage positive health behavior changes among students. Willing to seek help and ask questions when needed. Receive direction and constructive feedback in a positive manner. Ability to work independently and in a team setting when needed. Demonstrate skills of a self-motivator and have high levels of energy and enthusiasm. Eagerness to learn. Serve as a responsible role model to both on and off campus students and the community, representing ESU in a positive manner. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Additional Information: Health & Wellness department working 7-10 hours per week hours subject to change. $15.00 per hour. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
