    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8783?c=esu": {
      "title": "Athletics Equipment Room Student Worker",
      "description": "Athletics Equipment Room Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Athletics Equipment Room Student Worker United States | req8783 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search East Stroudsburg University’s Department of Athletics currently seeks a dynamic individual to serve as Athletics Equipment Room Student Worker. Successful candidates will work in collaboration with the equipment room staff and other department personnel members of the ESU Athletic Department. Job Summary: The Athletics Equipment Room Student Worker assists the Equipment Room with certain duties during practices, games, and in the equipment room as needed. The duties for this position within the ESU Athletic Department include but are not limited to the following: Perform traditional equipment room managerial duties, such as preparing for practices (setting up drills, equipment, etc.), operating the clock at practice, retrieving balls or equipment. Assist in coordination of equipment and apparel for competition. Assist in laundry services, cleaning, maintaining, and repairing equipment and protective clothing. Assist in maintaining accurate inventory controls for equipment and apparel. Assist in executing various home and away game day responsibilities as needed at the direction of the Athletics Equipment Manager or Graduate Assistant Equipment Manager. Ensure a safe, organized and professional experience at all times for coaches and players. Qualifications: Current ESU student in good academic standing. Be registered for the fall/spring semester. Ability to work any days and/or shifts needed, including nights and weekends. Ability to exercise sound judgment and solve problems as necessary and work well under pressure and in a fast paced environment. Must be available to work up to 20 hours per week. Applicants must be personable, reliable, have great communication skills, and have high levels of integrity and professionalism in all aspects of the role. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $9.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8782?c=esu": {
      "title": "Center for Student Engagement and Belonging Student Worker",
      "description": "Center for Student Engagement and Belonging Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Center for Student Engagement and Belonging Student Worker United States | req8782 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Center for Student Engagement and Belonging Student Worker As the Center for Student Engagement and Belonging Student Worker, you’ll help create a welcoming, inviting space for everyone who walks through our doors. You’ll support the team with front-desk coverage, jump in on center events, and assist staff with day-to-day projects. Responsibilities: Welcome fellow students and visitors and connect them with the right person or office. Answer phones and emails, help with basic questions, and take quick messages for the team. Keep things running smoothly with simple day-to-day office tasks like printing, data entry, scanning, and mail. Jump in on campus events by helping set up spaces, checking students in, and passing out gear or flyers. Keep the office and front desk area organized, and stocked with basic supplies. Team up with staff on fun projects, research, and extra tasks as they come up during the semester. Qualifications: Current ESU Student Hours: Ten hours per week, with the potential to 20 hours based on workload. Pay Rate: $9 per hour Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
