    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8780?c=esu": {
      "title": "Faculty Assistant Kinesiology EXER 202 for CRN 32686",
      "description": "Faculty Assistant Kinesiology EXER 202 for CRN 32686 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Faculty Assistant Kinesiology EXER 202 for CRN 32686 United States | req8780 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/24/2026 Back to Search Faculty Assistant for Kinesiology EXER 202 CRN 32686 The Program The Faculty Assistant (FA) program supports faculty who are teaching (three or four credit) classes of sixty (60) or more students (for classes of 120 or greater registered students, two FAs can be provided). The FA can assist faculty in any classroom activity deemed appropriate for 6 hours per week for 15 weeks at $9.00 per hour. Position Description Students participating in the East Stroudsburg University Faculty Assistant (LCA) program are required to attend all classes for which they are providing support. FAs will work directly with professors who will outline their position responsibilities which may include: verifying class rosters, taking  attendance, arranging for technology services, and assisting with  maintaining and uploading course materials and information onto D2L. Additionally, FAs can assist with proctoring exams, scanning, copying, collating, distributing course materials, and updating bulletin boards. The Faculty Assistant may be assigned other duties as directed by the professor that are appropriate, but may not perform any functions as instructor of record, e.g., LCAs are not to grade any course assignments. Required Qualifications: Current ESU Student. Hired or recommended by the professor who teaches the course. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8212?c=esu": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Analytical Chemistry",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Analytical Chemistry | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Analytical Chemistry United States | req8212 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/21/2026 Back to Search The\nDepartment of Chemistry and Biochemistry at East Stroudsburg University (ESU)\ninvites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor with a\nspecialty in analytical chemistry starting in August 2027. Appointment at the\nAssistant or Associate Professor level will be commensurate with qualifications\nand experience. For full consideration, applications will begin on September 28, 2026. The successful candidate will demonstrate highly effective teaching and\nenthusiasm for advising and mentoring a diverse population of undergraduate\nstudents. Primary responsibilities include teaching analytical chemistry and\nassociated laboratory courses. Additional teaching responsibilities may include\ngeneral chemistry, non-majors' courses, and upper-division offerings in the\ncandidate’s area of expertise. An active research program involving\nundergraduate students is expected. Faculty contribute to university service by\nparticipating in activities including committee memberships, curriculum\ndevelopment, and outreach. The Department's Chemistry and Biochemistry programs are accredited by the\nAmerican Chemical Society (ACS) and the American Society for Biochemistry and\nMolecular Biology (ASBMB). The department is located in the Hoeffner Science\nand Technology Center and houses 13 dedicated teaching and research\nlaboratories, a cold room, and modern faculty offices. The department maintains\nan impressive suite of instrumentation including a Bruker 400 MHz NMR, Agilent\nLC/Q-TOF Mass Spectrometer, GC/MS, HPLCs, IR, UV/Vis, and fluorescence spectrometer. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Chemistry, Biochemistry, or closely related field must be completed prior to appointment. Previous experience or\ndemonstrated ability to teach analytical chemistry and general chemistry is\npreferred. A record of peer-reviewed\npublications is highly desirable, as is experience in obtaining external\nfunding. Experience or interest in\ncurriculum and course development is advantageous. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and must include: (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of your teaching philosophy, (4) a research plan involving undergraduates, (5) a statement on your approach to inclusive teaching of a diverse student population and (6) unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts. Additional materials, including official transcripts and three letters of reference, will be requested from finalists. ABD candidates must provide authoritative documentation supporting Ph.D. conferral date. Only completed applications will receive consideration. ABD candidates must provide authoritative documentation\nsupporting Ph.D. conferral date prior to appointment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
