    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8764?c=esu": {
      "title": "College of Business & Management Data Analytics Intern",
      "description": "College of Business & Management Data Analytics Intern | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) College of Business & Management Data Analytics Intern United States | req8764 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/19/2026 Back to Search College of Business & Management Data Analytics Intern Job Summary: East Stroudsburg University is one\nof two institutions in Pennsylvania where students learn about and are\nseamlessly certified in data analytics through our exclusive partnership with\nSAS, Statistical Analysis Systems. ESU students who are pursuing the certification\nand/or minor are eligible to complete an internship where they can apply what\nthey have learned to create real world industry solutions. The Data Analytics\nIntern role is a project-based experiential learning opportunity with an ESU\nWork-Based Learning employer/partner. Major responsibilities include assisting\nthe site supervisor(s) with the organization and management of large data sets,\ncompleting tasks associated with data coding, collection, scrubbing, analysis,\nand visualization, and otherwise contributing to the data-driven\ndecision-making process. Work may involve collaboration as a team or\nindependent assignments that foster intellectual growth by active participation\nin the WBL employer’s/partner’s business operations. Duties: Through research, develop and maintain an\nunderstanding of the employer’s industry and needs. Assist the design and delivery of applications that focus on data\ncollection from various input sources ensuring that there is a quality\nmechanism in place for data collection and consistency in tracking. Review and analyze data from\nmultiple sources to create a cohesive, easy to understand situational presentation to support site supervisor. Utilize machine learning, modeling programs, and statistical\ntechniques to extract insights from various data sources. Develop reports to reinforce the site supervisors lead that emphasize relevant\ntrends, metrics and benchmarks that can highlight key performance indicators\nfor various focus areas. Create visualizations and storytelling with\ndata by developing business-related dashboards that appeal to target audiences’\ninterest and facilitate ease-of-use. Assist\nin generating solutions through data-driven insights. Understand and apply sound data governance practices. Participate\nin scoping data analytics projects. Document\nand train other data users as needed. Qualifications: Completing a bachelor’s degree that includes a\ndata analytics minor or certification coursework. Possesses an outstanding work ethic, a sense of urgency to\nmeet established deadlines, has good communication skills – listening with\nability to communicate clearly and concisely to others. Requires a semester long commitment with break weeks and\nscheduled vacation off. Proficient\nin Python, Power BI, SAS, Microsoft Office applications; web conferencing tools\nsuch as Zoom and Microsoft Teams; and social media platforms such as LinkedIn\nand Twitter. Experience working in a project-based environment with\neffective results of participation. Technical Skills: High proficiency using SAS and\nassociated SAS tools. High\nproficiency in use of a technical tool to organize, manage, analyze, and\nvisualize Additional Information: Hourly Rate of Pay $15 to $20 based on experience Up to 20 hours per week Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8729?c=esu": {
      "title": "Temporary Upward Bound Non-Credit Lecturer Foundations and Seminars",
      "description": "Temporary Upward Bound Non-Credit Lecturer Foundations and Seminars | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temporary Upward Bound Non-Credit Lecturer Foundations and Seminars United States | req8729 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/19/2026 Back to Search As the Non-Credit Lecturer for Foundations and Seminars you will need to think creatively and be comfortable working with a diverse student population. You will be an active member of the Upward Bound team and will work closely with the Director to help build high school student's skillset for higher education. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your teaching experience and excellent communication skills all while, propelling students towards success. To be successful in this role, you must be detail-oriented, creative, and have strong interpersonal skills. Your normal hours will be on Saturday's 8:30 AM to 3:00 PM but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true non-credit lecturer. This is a temporary grant funded role from August 28th, 2026, to May 8th, 2027. The role is continually contingent upon this grant funding. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the Upward Bound operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Co-teach courses\npertaining to financial aid / FAFSA. Aid students\nwith interpreting PSAT, SAT, and ACT results. Assist students\nin developing pre-college resumes. Conduct\nworkshops for students pertaining to leadership, learning styles, decision-making,\nand community service. Intervene and\ncounsel students as needed and report areas of concern to the program\nadministrative staff. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Bachelor’s degree in Psychology or related field. Master’s degree preferred Prior experience in TRIO Upward Bound or similar program preferred. Experience with local school districts preferred. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. What We Offer Salary: $28.00 Hourly Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8765?c=esu": {
      "title": "Histology Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Histology Lab Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Histology Lab Assistant United States | req8765 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/13/2026 Back to Search Histology Lab Assistant Job Summary: East Stroudsburg University’s Biological Sciences Dept. seeks a student to provide lab assistance for BIOL\n410: Histology. The student worker will attend the weekly lab sessions in Moore Biology 210, and assist the professor in helping students during lab activities.  Additionally, the lab assistant will hold open lab sessions, help to prepare materials for lab exercises, and organize lab supplies. Lab assistants may not perform any functions as instructor of record (e.g., grade any course assignments). Number of\nPositions: 1 Pay Rate: $9.00 Hours per\nWeek: 8-10 Supervisor: Dr. Samantha Gartner Anticipated\nStart Date: August 24, 2026 Anticipated\nEnd Date: May 15, 2027 Location: Moore Biology Room 210 Qualifications: A student\nworker must have previously completed this course with a grade of B or higher. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
