    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8762?c=esu": {
      "title": "Admissions Tour Guide",
      "description": "Admissions Tour Guide | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Admissions Tour Guide United States | req8762 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search Admissions Tour Guide Position Summary: Admission Ambassadors and Tour\nGuides are responsible for welcoming prospective students and families to ESU.\nAdmission Ambassadors will work with the office supporting the Admission staff to\nprepare and set up Admission events, lead campus tours, and help prospective\nstudents navigate their college journey. Responsibilities: Lead and guide prospective students and families on campus tours and identify important campus locations. Address concerns and questions from prospective students and their families. Participate in Admission events including Open Houses, Weekend Visit Day, Admitted Students Celebration, VIP lunch visits, Bus visits, and weekly campus tours. Share personal ESU experiences with prospective students and families. Connect families with their Admission staff. Prepare event materials, make event folders, and participate in event logistics. Qualifications: Be enrolled at ESU as a full-time student. Maintain a 2.50 cumulative and semester GPA. Be in good academic and judicial standing. Professionally represent ESU. Work well in group settings, with individuals, and maintain a positive attitude during work. Must be available for all of the Admission Events. Be a good public speaker. Be knowledgeable about ESU campus, events, and student experience. Compensation: $12 - $15 per hour based on experience. Duration: August 2026 – August 2027. Training: Training will occur during the first week on the job. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
