    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8758?c=esu": {
      "title": "Art+Media+ Design Art Gallery Monitor",
      "description": "Art+Media+ Design Art Gallery Monitor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Art+Media+ Design Art Gallery Monitor United States | req8758 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/10/2026 Back to Search Art+Media+Design Art Gallery Monitor Job Summary: The Art + Media + Design Gallery\nMonitor is expected to be in the gallery to greet visitors, watch over the art,\nand tend to duties that pertain to maintaining the gallery needs. Students who\nare hired in this role will represent the gallery professionally. Such responsibilities for gallery\nmonitors will be helping the gallery director, exhibition curators and exhibiting\nartists with installing and breaking down shows. Gallery monitors will be present\nduring hours as agreed. Responsibilities: Open gallery and the gates every day. Greet and monitor visitors in the gallery. Represent the department in all aspects in a professional manner. Help gallery director and exhibiting artists with installing and breaking down shows. Be a presence during Gallery hours as well as shows and exhibitions as agreed. Assisting the Administrative Assistant and Department Chair with various office tasks. Lock the gallery door and close the gates at the end of the day. Qualifications: Excellent customer service skills Must be professional. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail to ensure procedures are followed accurately. This is a full semester commitment, ability to attend all shows is must. Additional Information: Working Hours:  11:00 am to 4:00 pm Monday through Friday. This position will require 10-15\nhrs. weekly. Pay\nRate: Starting\nat $10.00 10-15 Hrs/week. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8757?c=esu": {
      "title": "Band Assistant",
      "description": "Band Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Band Assistant United States | req8757 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/10/2026 Back to Search Band\nAssistant Job Summary: Assist Band Director with keeping band room neat and organized and keep\ninventory of instruments and uniforms. Responsibilities: Inventory instruments Keep a full and ongoing record of all instruments and a thorough record of where each instrument is at all times. Inventory Uniforms Assist Band director is making copies of music, keeping music organized and filed properly. Assist Band director in contacting band members to relay information. Keep an updated schedule of where the Band will be expected to play and when. Qualifications: Excellent customer service skills Ability to work in a fast-paced environment Strong attention to detail to ensure procedures are followed\naccurately Reliability is a must; this is a full semester commitment. Working Hours: 8:00am – 8:00pm Monday through Friday. Pay\nRate: Starting at $10.00 10-15 Hrs/week Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8734?c=esu": {
      "title": "Applications Developer 1",
      "description": "Applications Developer 1 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Applications Developer 1 United States | req8734 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/10/2026 Back to Search As the Applications Developer 1, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable as a Subject Matter Expert for the Universities Ellucian Banner information system and network. You will be an active member of the Computing & Communications Services team and will work closely with the Senior Applications Developer to seamlessly integrate upgrades to support student learning and campus initiatives. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your information technology or coding background and application development experience all while troubleshooting to create comprehensive upgrades for the Student Information System (SIS) and integrated ancillary systems. To be successful in this role, you must demonstrate strong communication skills, proven problem-solving skills, and an extensive understanding of the modern application development life cycle. Your normal schedule will be Monday through Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Applications Developer 1. This role is 100% in-person employment here at ESU. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Design and implement web-based solutions for user access to administrative data and functions. Customize and implement portal and other vendor products Integrating existing systems with new systems. Participate in design and implementation of unified authorization system. Develop security scheme and maintenance mechanisms. Independent design and development of real-time and/or batch interfaces using application specific tools and/or web services. Meets with clients to determine manual or automated processing inefficiencies or problems, business objectives and operational needs, level of utilization of existing systems, and computer equipment capability to identify information technology alternatives and provide solutions for improving operations. Conducts detailed studies of the current system, including its procedures, information flows and methods of work organization and control to develop a logical model of the current system. Participates in the development of criteria to evaluate complex user applications and determine whether systems can be created using packaged desktop PC software or require traditional application development efforts. Serves as a team member on highly complex departmental systems development projects that involve critical business processes, numerous variables and diverse operational requirements. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Minimum Experience & Training: One year as an Information Technology Trainee or Computer Programmer 2. or One Year of Information Technology experience in applications development or application maintenance, and an associate’s degree in any information technology field. or Three years of information technology experience that includes two years of experience in applications development of applications maintenance. Technical Skills: 2+ years' experience with relational database and web development. Experience supporting users of computers and information systems. Knowledge of PC spreadsheets and database access tools. SQL programming experience required, Oracle Weblogic, C#, Insomina, Postman, Bruno, GITHub, and experience with both UNIX and Windows preferred. Preferred Systems Knowledge & Experience: Ellucian Ethos API Integrations (Spec-Based and Ellucian Partner). Ellucian Experience platform. Ellucian WorkFlow. Evisions ARGOS Reporting Environment. ISE Integrations and Job Scheduling. Ellucian Insights. Additional Requirements: Aptitude to think critically and apply critical thinking skills to solve problems independently; make independent decisions that support the needs of the University and its students. Able to quickly pivot between work tasks when unplanned events occur that need immediate attention. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $60,538 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8723?c=esu": {
      "title": "Facility Operations Supervisor - Electrical",
      "description": "Facility Operations Supervisor - Electrical | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Facility Operations Supervisor - Electrical United States | req8723 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/8/2026 Back to Search As the Facilities Operations Supervisor, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable overseeing all electrical system repairs and maintenance for campus buildings. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Manager of Energy and Mechanical Services creating proposals to ensure the upkeep of various electrical machinery. It is essential in this position that the candidate delivers excellent supervision to their team of dedicated employees from various journey-level trades. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your extensive electrical maintenance background and working experience, interpreting and executing blueprint plans for projects. In addition, this role requires the skilled implementation of comprehensive knowledge on national electrical best practices for campus services. To be successful in this role, the person must be highly organized, detail oriented, and able to work in a fast-paced environment. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Facilities Operations Supervisor. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Plans, supervises, schedules, and\nassigns work to various skilled tradesmen and sub-journeyman level employees\nperforming building maintenance and repair maintenance work. Evaluates, prioritizes, and\nassigns construction, renovation, installation, repair, and maintenance work\norders. Ensures all assignments are\ncompleted in compliance with trades methods, efficiency standards,\nmanufacturing guidelines, regulations, codes, and project objectives. Responsible for the repair and replacement of\nelectrical motors, controllers, switchboard panels, lights, power circuits, and\nelectrical generators. Perform skilled tasks per standard\npractices of the electrical trade and the National Electrical Code. Plan and lay-out the installation\nof conduits for power, lighting, signal, and fire alarm wires. Make estimates of time and\nmaterial, lay-outs, plans, and schedules work for the electricians and Maintenance Repairmen. Provides training and on-the-job\nguidance and assistance on the proper methods, techniques, tools, equipment,\nand safety precautions. Makes inspections of buildings and\ngrounds to determine and estimate costs of repairs and maintenance needed. Reads blueprints and\nspecifications for new construction or renovation projects and various maintenance\njobs; estimates materials and labor needed. Comply with hazard and safety\nprecautions of the electrical trade, work with high voltage, and ensure\nsubordinates follow proper safety precautions. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Minimum Qualifications: Five years of experience at the\njourney level divided among a minimum of two of the building, electrical, or\ntelephone, data trades at the supervisory level, or such training as may have\nbeen gained through graduation from high school or vocational school. Any equivalent combination of\nexperience and training. List functional requirements such as degrees, type of\nwork experience, certifications. Valid Drivers License. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of the standard\npractices, processes, equipment, tools, and materials involved in trades\nrelated to electrical trade and general building maintenance. Knowledge of occupational hazards\nand safety precautions of building maintenance and new construction or\nrenovation work. Ability to use, maintain, and care\nfor the tools and equipment employed in building maintenance and repair work. Knowledge of National Electric\nCode. Capability to plan, assign,\nsupervise, and evaluate the work of a varied group of skilled and semi-skilled\nworkers. Ability to train and instruct\nstaff on safety precautions and to provide guidance on the proper methods and\ntechniques for accomplishing skilled trades and building maintenance work. Knowledge to make and work from\nsketches or plans for improvement or alteration of buildings and equipment and\nto interpret blueprints and sketches Ability to make accurate estimates\nof time and materials required for repair and maintenance work. Experience preparing and maintaining appropriate records and reports. Thorough knowledge of methods,\nmaterials, tools, and practices of the electrical, telephone, and Data trades. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $53,008 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8165?c=esu": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Coordinator for the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for Students",
      "description": "Tenure Track Coordinator for the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for Students | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Coordinator for the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for Students United States | req8165 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/5/2026 Back to Search As the Tenure Track Coordinator for the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for Students (OASIS), you will oversee the implementation of accommodations and services for students with disabilities in accordance with Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) of 1990. You will review disability-related documentation, determine eligibility for services, and engage in the interactive process to establish individualized accommodations. In this role, you will provide leadership for the department by directing strategic planning, establishing and overseeing policies and procedures, managing budget planning and resource allocation, supervising staff, and using departmental data to support informed decision-making and continuous service improvement. You will work closely with the Chair of the department and campus partners to promote accessibility and ensure compliance with applicable disability laws and regulations. The successful candidate will bring a background in vocational rehabilitation, counseling, assistive technology, or a related field, along with experience in higher education disability services, staff supervision, and budget management. Your hours will be between Monday and Friday, 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM. You may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Coordinator for OASIS. This is a permanent tenure track 12-month position. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Directs strategic planning, administration, and coordination of multi-faceted service area and provides leadership and direction for the department. Reviews disability-related documentation and determines student eligibility for accommodations and services. Engages in the interactive process with students to determine individualized, reasonable accommodations. Coordinates and oversees the implementation of approved accommodations in collaboration with students, faculty, and relevant campus partners. Serves as academic advisor to students in OASIS. Manages all facets of the OASIS Testing Center. Plans, implements and evaluates projects and services related to student accommodations and accessibility throughout the university. Establishes, monitors, evaluates, and improves processes, procedures, and standards to provide service improvement for the disabled community. Directs and supervises the data collection and preparation of a variety of complex reports, statements, and communications. Makes recommendations impacting students, faculty, staff, programs, grants, and service providers or vendors. Develops, administers and monitors budgets. Allocates resources to benefits students, faculty, staff, and community members with disabilities. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Master’s degree in vocational rehabilitation, counseling, assistive technology or related field and a minimum of 2 years working in the areas of disability services in higher education. Understanding of relevant laws and regulations, such as the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Knowledge of physical, medical, psychological, sensory and learning disabilities and reasonable accommodations for such disabilities. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff. Efficient in managing multiple tasks and maintaining detailed records. Knowledge of adaptive equipment and technology (preferred). Ability to work with a complex data system such as Accommodate and Banner(preferred). Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: Based on Experience Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
