    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8748?c=esu": {
      "title": "Biological Sciences Undergraduate Intern",
      "description": "Biological Sciences Undergraduate Intern | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Biological Sciences Undergraduate Intern United States | req8748 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search Biological Sciences Undergraduate Intern Job Overview: The Plant Physiology Lab seeks a dedicated and\ndetail-oriented student worker to assist with a range of laboratory and\nresearch tasks. The ideal candidate will have a keen interest in plant\nphysiology and be willing to learn new techniques and protocols. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist with daily laboratory tasks including cleaning and\nmaintaining equipment, preparing solutions, and managing inventory of\nlaboratory supplies. Participate in setting up, conducting, and documenting\nexperiments under the supervision of the supervisor. Particularly,\nparticipate in transgenic plant production and maintenance after training. Use lab software for data entry, analysis, and\npresentation. Assist with the care and maintenance of plants in the lab\nand greenhouse. Follow all laboratory safety procedures and protocols. Attend lab meetings and contribute to discussions on\nresearch findings and project progress. Qualifications: Currently enrolled in a biology or related degree program\nat ESU. Prior lab experience or coursework involving plant\nbiology or physiology is preferred but not required. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Basic computer skills including familiarity with\nMicrosoft Office suite and ability to learn lab-specific software. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Must be able to lift, pull, or push up to 25 pounds and perform tasks\nrequiring manual dexterity. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $7.25 This position requires a commitment of at least 3 hours per\nweek. The schedule is flexible. Some weekend and evening hours may be required\ndepending on the needs of the laboratory. The Plant Physiology Lab Assistant is a valuable member of\nour research team. This position offers a unique opportunity to gain hands-on\nexperience in plant physiology research, working closely with faculty and\ngraduate students. We encourage all interested candidates to apply. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8747?c=esu": {
      "title": "Athletic Communications Student Worker",
      "description": "Athletic Communications Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Athletic Communications Student Worker United States | req8747 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search East Stroudsburg University’s Department of\nAthletics currently seeks a dynamic individual to serve as Student Worker for\nAthletic Communications: Job Summary: Successful candidates will work in collaboration with other student workers and department personnel as well as under the direction of the Assistant to the Athletic Director, Athletic Administration Graduate Assistants, and other members of the ESU Athletic Department. Description: The student worker for athletic operations helps to provide a safe, organized and professional game experience at all athletic events for fans, student-athletes, game officials and the ESU community. The student worker position, if assigned, also helps to maintain a safe and welcoming environment of Koehler Fieldhouse. The duties for this position within the ESU Athletic Department include but are not limited to the following: Assist with stats software during home sporting events Assist with the running of cameras and/or broadcast production software Serve as broadcaster/color commentor/public address announcer at events Assist with photography and video projects Assist with graphic design and video editing using the Adobe Creative Suite Assist with content creation for social media accounts Write game recaps and help update esuwarriors.com Qualifications: Current ESU student in good academic standing. Be registered for the fall/spring semester. Ability to work any days and/or shifts needed, including nights and weekends including Homecoming and Family weekend. Must be able to work both outside and inside events and tolerate variable weather conditions. Ability to exercise sound judgment and solve problems as necessary and w ork well under pressure and in a fast-paced environment. Must be available to work 10-20 hours per week. Applicants must be personable, reliable, have great communication skills, and have high levels of integrity and professionalism in both behavior and appearance. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8746?c=esu": {
      "title": "Campus Card Center Student Worker",
      "description": "Campus Card Center Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Campus Card Center Student Worker United States | req8746 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search Campus Card Center Student Worker The Student will report to the Director of the Campus Card Center and\nassist with the daily office functions of the Campus Card Center while\nproviding excellent customer service and responsiveness. The position may\nrequire some weekend or holiday hours based on the needs of the office. Responsibilities: Assist with maintaining day to day operations and facilitating a customer service-oriented environment. Assist with the daily production and distribution of ID Cards (eCards). Support maintaining campus card accounting procedures to ensure proper collection of funds. Participate in all campus training (Title IX and other programs) that promote a campus environment in which racial and ethnic differences are respected and appreciated. Maintain the privacy and confidentiality of all system and office-generated data, card transactions, and reports. Process all paperwork related to deposits, applications, and replacement eCards. Answer phone calls and questions from students and parents regarding the eCard. Qualifications: Current ESU Student Excellent customer service skills General knowledge of computers Strong problem-solving skills Ability to work in a fast-paced environment Communication skills to be able to assist customers over the phone Strong attention to detail to ensure procedures are followed accurately General knowledge of ESU’s campus is preferred, but not required Additional Information: Hourly rate $7.25 Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8745?c=esu": {
      "title": "Athletics Game Operations",
      "description": "Athletics Game Operations | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Athletics Game Operations United States | req8745 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search East\nStroudsburg University’s Department of Athletics currently seeks a dynamic\nindividual to serve as Student Worker for athletic game operations. Successful candidates\nwill work in collaboration with other student workers and department personnel\nas well as under the direction of the ESU Athletics Department. Job Duties: The\nstudent worker for athletic game operations helps to provide a safe, organized and professional game experience at all athletic\nevents for fans, student-athletes, game officials and the ESU community. The\nstudent worker position, if assigned, also helps to maintain a safe and\nwelcoming environment of Koehler Fieldhouse. The duties for this position\nwithin the ESU Athletic Department include\nbut are not limited to the following: Serve\n     as athletic event staff during athletic events in roles that could include\n     ball shagger, parking staff, scoreboard operator, videoboard operator,\n     music, usher, ticketing, concessions, and security. Assist\n     in executing various game day responsibilities at the direction of the\n     game operations supervisor. Assist\n     in the setup and break down of athletic events. Assist\n     in facility management, athletic administration and office\n     responsibilities as requested. Assist\n     with in-game, event promotions and community engagement. Provide\n     excellent customer service and a positive environment to all fans, teams,\n     and officials at athletic events. Ensure\n     a safe, organized and professional experience at all times. Qualifications: Current ESU student in good academic standing. Be registered for the fall/spring semester. Ability to work any days and/or shifts needed, including nights and weekends including Homecoming and Family weekend. Must be able to work both outside and inside events and tolerate variable weather conditions. Ability to exercise sound judgment and solve problems as necessary and work well under pressure and in a fast paced environment. Must be available to work 10-20 hours per week. Applicants must be personable, reliable, have great\n     communication skills, and have high levels of integrity and\n     professionalism in both behavior and appearance. Additional Information: Hourly pay $9.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8744?c=esu": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician Student Worker",
      "description": "Laboratory Technician Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Laboratory Technician Student Worker United States | req8744 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search Laboratory Technician Student Worker The Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife Genetics Institute is seeking student\nworkers in our vector borne disease laboratory, testing ticks submitted to the\nlaboratory for disease agents, traveling to field sites to collect ticks and\nidentification of ticks. This is a unique opportunity to support research on\nvector borne disease. The candidate will perform a variety of functions in support\nof the research group. Primary duties will involve projects that are focused on\nthe evaluation of RNA/DNA, handling, identifying, and storing samples and assisting\nwith qPCR sample testing. The student work will also be responsible for\ncleaning and calibrating equipment, measuring compounds and preparing solutions\nfor use. Responsibilities Adherence to laboratory safety procedures and Standards of Practice are essential. Clean and calibrate scientific equipment. Assist Laboratory Technicians with carrying out tests using scientific techniques, such as DNA extractions, polymerase chain reaction and gel electrophoresis. Inputting data into computer programs.. Analyzing and interpreting data. Identifying and testing ticks for various tick-borne pathogens. Required Skills Understanding of DNA extraction and Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is preferred. Successful candidates will be self-motivated, organized, independent, and eager to learn a breadth of techniques. Occasional evening and/or weekend work will be required. Must have excellent critical thinking, problem solving, verbal and written skills, deductive reasoning and highly perceptive and detail-oriented. Successful candidate must work well in small and large groups. Current ESU student pursuing a bachelors or graduate degree in biological sciences, or related degree, with an overall GPA of 3.0 or higher. Hours: 20 hours a week Pay: $12.00 per hour Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8695?c=esu": {
      "title": "Conference Services and Events Manager",
      "description": "Conference Services and Events Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Conference Services and Events Manager United States | req8695 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/3/2026 Back to Search As the Conference Services & Events Manager, you will need to successfully spearhead all stages from the strategic planning to the skillful execution of campus events, meetings, or conferences for the Campus Community. You will be an active member of the Economic Development & Entrepreneurship team and will work closely with the Director of the University Center to create a streamlined process in partnership with internal stakeholders centered around memorable experiences that enhance the impact of campus congregation. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your extensive progressive management of events and excellent collaboration skills all while effectively overseeing departmental budgets. To be successful in this role, you must possess strong organizational skills, experience managing scheduling platforms, and the ability to seamlessly pivot between tasks. This\nposition is primarily Monday through Friday during standard business hours.\nOccasional evening, weekend, and extended hours are required to support\nconferences, meetings, and special events. There is up to 10% travel to local locations for this role. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Operational Management: Oversee daily operations,\nincluding scheduling, staff supervision, and on-site troubleshooting for\nevents. Manage, build out and maintain\naccurate content in a centralized scheduling system for events, meetings, and public\nspace reservations. Work with vendors (caterers,\ndecorators, speakers) to ensure services meet contractual obligations. Recruit, train and manage student\nworkers, interns, volunteers prior to and during events. Maintain database of\npersonnel and contact information for follow up. Prepare pre- and post-event\nanalysis and assess opportunities and make recommendations for improving\nservice to internal and external constituencies and implement those\nimprovements as appropriate. Collaborate with the College of Business\nand Management to identify and engage students enrolled in the Hospitality,\nRecreation and Tourism Management Events. Prepare post event reports to\ninclude reflection and suggestions for next year’s event. Also, prepare\nyear-end events report, providing overall department analysis. Manage all aspects of conferences,\nworkshops, and ceremonies. Manage all aspects of food service\nand catering in collaboration with the University food service provider and\ncatering vendors as related to event management. Ensure seamless coordination of AV,\nsetup, technical, and security needs for campus events. Budgeting & Invoicing: Develop event budgets, handle\nvendor engagement, manage billing, and process invoices. Prepare, manage, and monitor event\nbudgets, anticipating costs of production, technical, and promotional needs,\nand set-up inventory. Ensure compliance with university and foundation\naccounting, audit and fiscal controls. Facility Dining & Inventory Oversight: Work with Facilities Management personnel to ensure meeting spaces, lounges, and guest rooms are prepared, clean, and meet standards. Safety & Compliance: In collaboration with campus police, ensure events adhere to university policies, health and safety regulations, and risk assessment protocols. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Bachelor's degree required in related field. A minimum of 5 to 8 years of\nexperience in substantial and progressively responsible planning, production\nand management of a variety of events from informal to formal, both large and\nsmall, ability to formulate creative ideas, and to analyze, evaluate, and\nnegotiate details reflective of a successful event. Excellent communication skills\nsufficient to express ideas and agreements concisely and persuasively, both\norally and in writing, to a variety of constituencies. Computer skills with\nability to use word processing and spreadsheet software, and knowledge of\ndesktop production and database systems. Valid Driver’s license required. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s Degree in a related field Demonstrated experience working\nwith event management, scheduling and design software including Social Tables, Course\ndog, EMS, etc. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: Based on Experience Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8743?c=esu": {
      "title": "Athletics Lifeguard 2026-2027",
      "description": "Athletics Lifeguard 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Athletics Lifeguard 2026-2027 United States | req8743 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/30/2026 Back to Search East\nStroudsburg University’s Department of Athletics currently seeks a dynamic\nindividual to serve as Student Lifeguard for Athletics Successful candidates\nwill be responsible for ensuring the safety of all adults and students using\nthe aquatic facility in Koehler Field House. Candidates will monitor activities\nin the swimming pool area, provide assistance to swimmers, inspect the\nfacilities for cleanliness and safety, and discharge related lifeguarding\nresponsibilities as per lifeguarding regulations. Job Duties: The\nstudent lifeguard for athletics helps to maintain a safe and welcoming environment of\nKoehler Fieldhouse Natatorium. The candidate will respond quickly,\nintelligently, decisively and in accordance with established emergency and\naccident management procedures. The duties for this position within the ESU\nAthletic Department include\nbut are not limited to the following: Maintains constant surveillance of patrons using the aquatics facility. Act immediately and appropriately to secure the safety of patrons in the event of an emergency. Follow ESU’s safety protocols and provide emergency care and treatment as required until the arrival of emergency medical services. (EMT’s, Campus Police and/or Athletic Trainers) React calmly and effectively in emergency situations. Provides courteous, friendly and professional assistance and maintain a high standard of customer service. Act as the liaison between patrons and athletic department staff in absence of Aquatics Coordinator. Qualifications: Current ESU student in good academic standing. Be registered for the fall/spring semester. Current Red Cross Lifeguard Training Certification. Current First Aid/AED/CPR for the Professional Rescuer. Previous lifeguard experience, preferred. Knowledge of current pool procedures, policies, rules and regulations governing the conduct of patrons using the pool and surrounding area. Ability to work any days and/or shifts needed, including nights and weekends. Ability to exercise sound judgment and solve problems as necessary and work well under pressure and in a fast paced environment. Applicants must be personable, reliable, have great\n     communication skills, and have high levels of integrity and\n     professionalism at all times in every aspect of the position. Additional Information: Hourly rate of pay $9.50 to $10.00 based on experience. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8742?c=esu": {
      "title": "English Student Worker",
      "description": "English Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English Student Worker United States | req8742 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/28/2026 Back to Search The English Department Is searching for a Motivated Student Worker Responsibilities: Provide general clerical and\noffice support for the department's faculty and administrative assistant. Tasks\ninclude fielding general questions from students, photocopying, filing and\ncollating documents.  p Performing general clerical tasks within a\nprofessional office setting. In addition, responsibilities include but are not\nlimited to assisting with departmental events and activities and supporting\ninitiatives necessary for the department's successful day-to-day operation. Required: Basic\nproficiency with basic office technologies. Strong interpersonal and\nproblem-solving skills. Pay Rate: $10 hourly Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
