    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8741?c=esu": {
      "title": "Physical Education General Office Aid",
      "description": "Physical Education General Office Aid | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Physical Education General Office Aid United States | req8741 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/28/2026 Back to Search The Physical Education Teacher Education (PETE) department is hiring a General Office Aide! Job Summary: We are seeking an organized General Office Aide\nto join our department.  The ideal\ncandidate will provide essential clerical support to ensure the smooth\noperation of our office.  This role\ninvolves a variety of tasks including front desk coverage, phone management,\nerrands and project assistance. Key Responsibilities: Front Desk Coverage-Greet students and visitors, manage the front desk, and provide a welcoming environment. Phone Management-Answer incoming call, take messages, and direct calls as appropriate Errands-Run errands around campus, including picking up and dropping off print request. Project Assistance-Work on various projects as assigned by faculty and staff. Information Updates-Update student information, TEC and scholarship boards regularly. Faculty Support-Assist faculty members with administrative tasks as needed. Qualifications: Strong organizational and multitasking skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Working conditions: Part-time position up to 20 hours per week. Office environment with occasional campus errands. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8740?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Graphics Center/Student Activity Assoc. 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Graphics Center/Student Activity Assoc. 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Graphics Center/Student Activity Assoc. 2026 - 2027 United States | req8740 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/27/2026 Back to Search POSITION DESCRIPTION Position Title: Graphics\nCenter Graduate Assistant Department: ESU Student\nActivity Association, Inc. (SAA) Reports to: Director of\nStudent Involvement & Leadership Development Position Type: Graduate Assistant (20 hours/week; academic-year appointment) POSITION SUMMARY The Graphics\nCenter Graduate Assistant supports day-to-day operational leadership for the SAA\nGraphics Center, a self-service creative and print-production space in the new\nUniversity Center. The Graduate Assistant manages the Center's operations,\nsupervises its student staff, and helps visiting students make effective use of\nself-service creative tools such as Canva and the Adobe Creative Suite. The\nposition is ideal for a graduate student who combines strong customer-service\nand organizational skills with an interest in creative and design technology. RESPONSIBILITIES Operations & Service Support daily operation of the Graphics Center, ensuring a welcoming, well-run, and professional environment. Manage the print-production workflow across both walk-in and online (WarriorLink) channels, including order triage, turnaround communication, and quality control. Assist with maintenance equipment (printers, laminator, cutter) and self-service workstations; track and reorder supplies. Ensure consistent cashless-payment processes, and serve as a point of contact for Center service questions. Maintain the Center's external-vendor resource binder for specialty items outside its production capabilities. Creative-Tool Support &\nSupervision Assist visiting students in navigating self-service tools (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite) — providing guidance rather than performing design work on their behalf. Directly supervise Graphics Center student staff, including scheduling, training, and performance management. Ensure adherence to ESU Licensing & Branding Guidelines. Administrative Assist the Director with budget tracking, reporting, and assessment of Center usage and service quality. Perform other related duties as assigned by the Director. REQUIREMENTS Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment in a graduate program at East Stroudsburg University, in good academic standing. Strong organizational, time-management, and customer-service skills. Comfort with, or willingness to learn, Canva, the Adobe Creative Suite, and print-production workflows. Ability to work independently and manage a service space with minimal supervision. Preferred Qualifications Experience or coursework in graphic design, digital media, communications, or a related creative field. Prior supervisory, leadership, or customer-service experience. Physical Requirements: Ability to sit or stand for\nextended periods, lift up to 25 pounds occasionally, and operate\nprint-production equipment. Accommodations\ncan be requested through the Office of Accessible Services Individualized for\nStudents (OASIS). COMPENSATION & ORGANIZATION This position is a graduate assistantship offering a stipend\nand tuition waiver in accordance with ESU’s graduate assistantship guidelines.\nSpecific details are available through the Office of Graduate Admissions and\nExtended Studies. About East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania East Stroudsburg University (ESU) is a comprehensive\nuniversity in northeastern Pennsylvania offering more than 50 undergraduate\nprograms, 21 master’s degree options, and two doctoral programs. It is one of\nthe 10 institutions in Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. Founded\nin 1893, ESU enrolls approximately 5,884 undergraduate and graduate students.\nLocated in the Pocono Mountains region, the university is less than two hours\nfrom both New York City and Philadelphia. SAA Mission Statement “The Student Activity Association, Incorporated (SAA), a\nuniversity affiliate, is dedicated to the support of East Stroudsburg\nUniversity students and the campus community.  This is accomplished by\nfostering active leaders for a global society and by providing innovative\nprograms, services, and initiatives to cultivate a holistic student\nexperience.” Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
