    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8248?c=esu": {
      "title": "Audio Visual Support Student Worker",
      "description": "Audio Visual Support Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Audio Visual Support Student Worker United States | req8248 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/15/2026 Back to Search Audio Visual Support Student Worker Job Summary: The students in this role will serve as support for the Audio-Visual team at ESU with the potential to do up to 20 hours per week of work. The starting pay for the role is $11 an hour but could be more based on your experience. Job Duties: Performs technical functions related to studio operation for productions in the television studio which includes: Audio, including setting up and use of audio boards, microphones, and audio feeds. Assist with camera trolley operation along with the Master control operations. Support the team through the use of Teleprompter operation. Operate and maintain electronic field video productions. Edit videos for the university using Final Cut Pro & Adobe Premiere. Archive all current videos and VHS tapes. Classroom support. Troubleshoot AV issues. Assist with maintaining AV equipment and Inventory. Aid in the installation of AV equipment. Event support with o perating audio and lighting during events. Qualifications: Current ESU Student Ability to lift, pull, carry, or move up to 50 pounds. Reliable and aptitude to learn the fundaments of audio visual computing. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8722?c=esu": {
      "title": "Faculty Assistant for SOCI 111: Intro to Sociology CRN 32431 & 33000",
      "description": "Faculty Assistant for SOCI 111: Intro to Sociology CRN 32431 & 33000 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Faculty Assistant for SOCI 111: Intro to Sociology CRN 32431 & 33000 United States | req8722 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/14/2026 Back to Search Faculty Assistant for Intro to Sociology 111: CRN 32431 & 33000 Job Summary: Faculty Assistants (FA) provide in class and out of class support to faculty who are teaching classes with over 60 students enrolled. The FA attends all classes for which they are providing support and work with professors who outline position responsibilities, which may include: verifying class rosters, taking attendance, arranging for technology services, and assisting with maintaining and uploading course materials and information onto D2L. The FA may also assist with scanning, copying, collating, distributing course materials, and updating bulletin boards. The FA may not perform any function s as the instructor of record or as a teaching assistant, e.g., the LCAs is not to lecture or to grade any course assignments. An LCA is hired by the professor for the course. Pay rate: $9.00 per hour. FA responsibilities include: Attends all classes for which they are providing support. Works with professors who will outline position responsibilities. Responsibilities may include: verifying class rosters, taking attendance, arranging for technology services, and assisting with maintaining and uploading course materials and information onto D2L. May also assist with scanning, copying, collating, distributing course materials, and updating bulletin boards. Note: The FA may not perform any functions as the instructor of record or as a teaching assistant, e.g., the FAs is not to lecture or to grade any course assignments or tutor students who are enrolled in the course. Required Qualifications: 1. Be enrolled at East Stroudsburg University 2. Be hired or recommended by the professor who teaches the course Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
