    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8639?c=esu": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper Supervisor",
      "description": "Groundskeeper Supervisor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Groundskeeper Supervisor United States | req8639 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/12/2026 Back to Search As the Groundskeeper Supervisor, you will need to think diligently planning and executing skilled work to maintain campus grounds, landscape construction, athletic field preparation, and snow removal operations. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Director to ensure campus layout is safe for the campus community during each season. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your landscaping background and strong working knowledge of equipment & vehicle maintenance all while skillfully operating single-chassis trucks or large-scale vehicles. To be successful in this role, you must possess experience in manicuring grounds, supervisory experience, and strong communication skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 7:00 am to 3:00 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule to work from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Groundskeeper Supervisor. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Supervises four (4)\nequipment operators, seven (7) groundskeepers and five (5) to ten (10) student\nsummer workers. Supervision of employees includes ensuring staff is assigned\nwork, reviews leave requests and performs annual reviews. Operate\nsingle-chassis trucks with a gross vehicle weight between 17,000 and 32,000\npounds to transport materials, supplies, and equipment to and from campus\nmaintenance and construction sites. Performs\nand directs staff regarding snow removal and ice control operations, including\nplowing, salting, cindering, and related winter weather response duties. Pulls\nwork orders, schedules assignments and closes work orders accordingly. Maintains\na pesticide license and applies pesticides as needed. Perform manual labor and grounds maintenance\nactivities when not operating equipment. Plan\n(layout and procuring), plant, maintain, and care for flowers, shrubs, grass\nseed, sod, and other landscape materials. Prepare\nand maintain athletic and recreational fields by lining fields, mowing,\nfertilizing, spraying, and performing other related turf maintenance duties\nnecessary for competitions and campus activities. Conduct\nroutine preventive maintenance and minor repairs on assigned equipment and\nvehicles, including cleaning, servicing, and maintaining operational records. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Valid\ndriver’s license without restrictions. Six\n(6) months of experience operating and maintaining single-chassis trucks with a\ngross vehicle weight between 17,000 and 32,000 pounds and/or construction and\nmaintenance equipment such as rollers, tractor-maintainers, excavators,\nfront-loaders, hi-lifts, and ground maintenance equipment; or an equivalent\ncombination of experience and training. Ability\nto safely operate heavy equipment, ground maintenance machinery, and motor\nvehicles in a variety of weather and terrain conditions. Perform physically demanding work, including lifting, carrying, pushing,\npulling, bending, standing, and walking for extended periods of time. Understand and follow written and verbal instructions. Ability\nto work independently while also functioning effectively within a team\nenvironment. Maintain effective working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and\nthe public. Ability\nto assign and perform snow removal and emergency response duties as assigned. Basic\nknowledge of preventive maintenance and minor repair procedures for equipment\nand vehicles. Ability\nto work outdoors in varying seasonal and environmental conditions, including\nexposure to noise, dust, fumes, and inclement weather. Maintain\na pesticide license. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $41,506 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8675?c=esu": {
      "title": "Parking Department Student Worker",
      "description": "Parking Department Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Parking Department Student Worker United States | req8675 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/6/2026 Back to Search University Police are searching for a Student Worker to support their Parking Team Job summary/basic function: Provide customer service to the campus community regarding parking and vehicle registration. Issue parking permits. Students in this position will be trained to operate the computer systems, phone lines, and radio dispatch. Students will be responsible for providing accurate information regarding parking. Required qualifications: Able to follow directions, multitask, answer phones, radio dispatch, no prior disciplinary incidents on campus. Current ESU Student. Hours per week: 8-10 (Part Time) Position status: Fall 2026 Location: 161 Smith Street, ground floor Hourly Rate: $10.00 \"Employment Eligibility and University Commitment\" Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8549?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Frederick Douglass Institute 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Frederick Douglass Institute 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Frederick Douglass Institute 2026 - 2027 United States | req8549 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/1/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: The Graduate Assistant with the Frederick Douglass Institute working 10 - 20 hours per week/150 - 300 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: Successful candidate should have a track record of experience working\nwith diverse populations and issues. Must also be self-motivated and have the focus to work on\nmultiple project simultaneously. The mission of the Frederick\nDouglass Institute at ESU is to promote campus diversity at all levels.  The\n2026-2027 Douglass Graduate Assistant will divide his/her work between several\ndifferent diversity initiatives including the Frederick Douglass Institute itself\n(posting on social media and attending both FDI meetings and campus events), the\nScholar program (student and faculty), Book Club (in conjunction with CMA),\nCreative Expression (in conjunction with the annual Student Summit in April of\neach year), Debate Society (state level competition held annually), and invited\nparticipation on the Diversity and Inclusion Committee at ESU. Responsibilities: The graduate assistant will aid with the roll out\nof the new program initiatives that include our student scholar program,\ncreative expression event, and book club. In addition, assistance with the\nfaculty scholar program will be needed when events are scheduled and campus\nwide events that are sponsored by FDI will need to be attended by the GA. The\nFrederick Douglass Debate society which is a unique opportunity for students to\nlearn, or enhance, public speaking skills will continue and require assistance\nwith advertising and promotion, including attendance at club fair, involvement\nfair, and open houses when possible. Posting on social media will be a necessary\npart of the job so that we can successfully advertise and promote the program\nwithin our own institution and across PASSHE as a whole. The successful\ncandidate will be required to attend executive committee meetings once a month\nand upon the needs of these smaller subgroups  - students scholars, faculty scholar, book club, debate, and creative\nexpression – assist in successful execution of events on campus for each. If interested but would\nlike to know more before applying, any interested potential GA can email Dr\nLaura Kieselbach: lkieselbac@esu.edu. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8499?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Research Assistant/Program Assistant 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Research Assistant/Program Assistant 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Research Assistant/Program Assistant 2026 - 2027 United States | req8499 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/1/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant Research Assistant/Program Assistant working 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: Assist faculty members in research and professional duties. Responsibilities : Assist Graduate Program Director (MS: AT) with the maintenance of program\nrecords, affiliation agreements, site visitations, and related standards in\npreparation for accreditation Assist the MS Program Director with the collection and analysis of\nstudent, site and clinical preceptor evaluations. Organize, analyze and publish\nassessment data for annual reports (middle states and AT accrediting agencies) Assist in the preparation of research laboratory for data collection\nprocedures Assist faculty members in the collection of data related to research\nstudies Coordinate with faculty and fellow graduate students in developing\nresearch projects/programs Perform other duties as assigned by Graduate Coordinator Required\nQualifications: Required:  Act 34 (PA Criminal\nBackground Clearance) Required:  Act 114 (FBI Criminal\nBackground Clearance: Fingerprinting) Required:  Act 151 (Child Abuse\nHistory Clearance) Required:  Professional Liability\nInsurance Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which con