      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Exercise Science Part-time 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Exercise Science Part-time 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Exercise Science Part-time 2026 - 2027 United States | req8427 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/1/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant with the Exercise Science department working 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: The Graduate Assistant with the Exercise Science department will assist in various laboratory functions and other administrative duties. Responsibilities: Laboratory Support Equipment maintenance Laboratory set-up and break down Research data collection Preparation of manuscripts and presentations Advanced technology integration Academic accreditation support Required Qualifications: Acceptance in M.S. in Clinical Exercise Physiology or M.S. in Exercise Science program Preferred Qualifications: Laboratory and research experience Computer skills Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8396?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics Men's Soccer Graduate Assistant 2026-2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics Men's Soccer Graduate Assistant 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics Men's Soccer Graduate Assistant 2026-2027 United States | req8396 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant with Athletics/Men's Soccer working 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: Serve as an assistant to the coaching staff. Assist with on-site supervision during all practices and competitions. Assist in the overall operating and planning of practice and competition. Assist with computer and video analysis. Assist with community engagement activities and fund raising projects. Assist with individuals and strength and conditioning program. Assist with academic study tables. Assist with recruiting qualified student athletes. Assist with instruction and training. Specific job responsibilities for the Graduate Assistantship position will be outlined further during the interview process. Required Qualifications: Admission to East Stroudsburg University. Graduate school application may occur at the same time as applying for the position. A Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. Criminal background check Ability to work nights and weekends Computer competency Driver’s license Excellent communication skills Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
