    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8671?c=esu": {
      "title": "Business Management Student Worker",
      "description": "Business Management Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Business Management Student Worker United States | req8671 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Business Management Student Worker Job Summary: The student worker will make copies; assist faculty members with attendance sheets; deliver important documents to other departments, and will have other duties assigned by the department secretary or department chair or other faculty members. Resume and references are required . Traits needed in this role are dependable, personable, hardworking, courteous, and professional. Job Requirements: Be a current ESU student. Non-Business Management student preferred. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8634?c=esu": {
      "title": "CILLS Fall & Spring Student Mentor 2026-2027",
      "description": "CILLS Fall & Spring Student Mentor 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) CILLS Fall & Spring Student Mentor 2026-2027 United States | req8634 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search CILLS Fall & Spring Student Mentor East Stroudsburg University's Career, Independent Living and Learning Studies (CILLS) Program through the Department of Special Education and Rehabilitation is currently seeking dynamic individuals to serve as their Student Mentors to provide support and learning experiences to individuals with intellectual disabilities. The Student Mentors will be responsible for: Providing support and learning experiences to individuals with intellectual disabilities. Supporting the students from 4:00PM-9:00PM on weekdays with socialization, academic, and daily living skills. For example, chores, cooking, attending campus events, completing homework, studying, etc. Supporting the students from 11:00AM-4:00PM or 4:00PM-9:00PM on weekends with socialization, academic, and daily living skills. For example, chores, cooking, attending campus events, completing homework, studying, etc. Supporting the students in making good and healthy decisions on their own. Reporting any incidents that happen during their shift with the students to the CILLS Staff. Documenting what they did during their shift with the students. The safety and wellbeing of the students during their shift. Additional Information: Student Mentors will work 10-20 hours per week - hours are flexible and may include day and/or evening shifts, and weekends. Saturday rotation is required. $10.00 per hour For more information call 570-422-3310 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8632?c=esu": {
      "title": "Chemistry Research Assistant",
      "description": "Chemistry Research Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Chemistry Research Assistant United States | req8632 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Chemistry Research Assistant Responsibilities: Assist the Principal Investigator (PI) with laboratory experiments, sample preparation, data collection, and analysis in support of ongoing chemistry research projects. Maintain accurate research records, follow laboratory safety protocols, and contribute to project goals. Qualifications: Must be current ESU Student Flexible hours are available to accommodate academic schedules. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $10 to $13 an hour based on experience \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8630?c=esu": {
      "title": "Global Relations Student Mentor",
      "description": "Global Relations Student Mentor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Global Relations Student Mentor United States | req8630 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Global Relations Student Mentor Job\nSummary: A Global\nRelations Peer Mentor is an experienced and thoughtful student leader who is\ncommitted to investing one’s time to assist in the growth and development of\nothers. The mentor is willing to share their knowledge, experience, and wisdom\nand act as a guide and role model. A peer mentor supports and encourages the\nacademic and social development of their mentees and provides active support to\nhelp them with adjusting to the ESU/college environment. The peer mentor offers\na fresh perspective and an independent point of view, while helping the mentee\nto succeed. The Global\nRelations Peer Mentor program is seeking peer mentors for the upcoming academic\nyear. As the Global Relations Peer Mentor, you will help guide a group of\napproximately 30+ new international students during their first year at ESU.\nThis connection begins during the semester before the student enrolls at ESU\nand works in tandem with the Student Success Coaches throughout the year. The\nprimary mission of the Global Relations Peer Mentor Program is to ease the\ntransition of new international students to East Stroudsburg University so that\nthey may succeed personally, socially, and academically. Additionally, the\nprogram helps each new international student connect with other students, the\nfaculty, student organizations, and staff offering support resources, and\nultimately the institution as a whole. Job\nDuties: Be a primary contact person for an\nexchange student and will provide information and guidance. Serve as a cultural guide. Help an exchange student to transition\ninto life at ESU. Become acquainted with all students in their\ngroup and other new students and establish positive relationships. Contact\nthe new student (usually via email) while still in his/her home university,\nimmediately after being matched. Provide the student with an idea of\nwhat is expected of an ESU student and to share tips about navigating the\ncampus. To help refer exchange students to\nsomeone on campus who is able to provide specific information when needed. Set positive examples for others in personal,\nacademic, and social behavior. Help build rapport each time he or she meets\nwith a mentee. Offer opportunities to solve problems and\nexchange ideas. Provide feedback that is honest, open and\npositive. Present opportunities to the mentee that he/she\nmay not have recognized on his/her own. Provide suggestions to the best of one’s\nknowledge that help the mentee succeed in the program. Participate in all the cultural events\nand stude nt engagement activities planned by the Study Abroad Services program for\nexchange students and buddies. Discuss and monitor engagement for each of the assigned mentees\nbased on expectations outlined by the Associate Provost for Student Success. Schedule, facilitate and prepare summaries of weekly\nmeetings with your group and submit them in a timely manner to the Associate\nProvost for Student Success. Maintain individual mentor hours that need to be\nlogged timely. Track attendance for all events and meetings. Contact the Associate Provost for Student\nSuccess immediately when faced with situations that the mentor cannot handle. Connect at least bi-weekly with your Student\nSuccess Coach in your college for triage on student cases. Job\nRequirements: Have and maintain a 2.75 GPA during the time of\nappointment. Successfully completed a Study Abroad – Outgoing\nExperience. Remain free of disciplinary sanctions. Complete the training modules for the Peer\nMentor certification and the Study Abroad Services program. Current ESU Student in good academic and disciplinary\n     standing. Basic computer skills. Experience in customer service. Ability to skillfully complete clerical work. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $13.00 Note: Students will receive a digital badge at the end of their first semester as a Global Relations Peer Mentor. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8609?c=esu": {
      "title": "Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing",
      "description": "Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing United States | req8609 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Maintenance Repairman 2, you will need to be comfortable repairing and maintaining the plumbing systems, HVAC equipment, piping systems, and associated equipment. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Facilities Operations Supervisor to complete routine tests to maintain steam lines. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your plumbing background with your excellent diagnostic skills all while timely executing requests to meet the needs of the ESU campus community. To be successful in this role, you must have strong attention to detail, problem- solving and technical skills. Your normal schedule will be Tuesday to Saturday 3:00 pm to 11:00 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Maintenance Repairman 2 . When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Employ established trade practices to install, repair, and do preventive maintenance on plumbing fixtures, HVAC systems, and other related equipment. Install, maintain , and repair valves, faucets, traps, sinks, and other sanitary fixtures. Maintain piping systems by opening clogged pipes and traps, repairing broken or leaking pipes, repairing steam lines. Repair and or replace circulating pumps and backflow valves in the heating system. Bend, cut, and solder copper pipe and tubing; cut, ream, and thread steel pipe; cut and glue plastic pipe. Changes HVAC filters and maintains HVAC equipment and controls. Repair and replace electrical motors, controllers, switchboard panels, lights, power circuits, and electrical generators. Locate and correct power failures and short circuits, install open and concealed wiring and lighting fixtures. Install temporary wiring for special events that are held at various locations on campus. Maintain working knowledge of the use of the standard tools, equipment, and testing devices of the electrical trade. Operate trade equipment such as drills, hammers, testing equipment, hand tools, scaffolding, bench grinder, right angle grinder saline saw, saw, cherry picker/manlift. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Four years of experience in the plumbing and electrical trade, or completion of an approved apprenticeship; or any equivalent combination of experience and training. Able to think critically and apply critical thinking skills to solve problems independently. Able to quickly pivot between work tasks when unplanned events occur that need immediate attention. Valid PA Driver’s License. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel , Teams required . What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $41,506 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8551?c=esu": {
      "title": "Computing and Communication Services Student Worker",
      "description": "Computing and Communication Services Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Computing and Communication Services Student Worker United States | req8551 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Computing and Communication Services Student Worker Job Summary: The Student IT Support Assistant\nprovides support to the Computing and Communication Services Center by\nassisting with a variety of technical and administrative tasks. This role\noffers hands-on experience in information technology, supporting daily operations,\ntroubleshooting, and departmental projects. Responsibilities: Assist with\nbasic coding and programming tasks as assigned. Support\nnetwork-related activities, including setup and troubleshooting of devices. Provide\naudiovisual technology (AVT) support for classrooms, meetings, and events. Help with\ninstallation, maintenance, and configuration of computer hardware and software. Perform\nadministrative duties such as filing, mail distribution, run errands. Assist IT\nstaff with ongoing projects and technical initiatives. Maintain a\nprofessional and customer-focused approach when providing support. Qualifications: Current ESU\nstudent in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field\npreferred Basic\nknowledge of computer systems, networking, or programming concepts Strong\nproblem-solving and communication skills Ability to\nwork independently and as part of a team Willingness to\nlearn new technologies and systems Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull light equipment between campus locations. Additional Information: $15.00 hourly pay Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8505?c=esu": {
      "title": "Peer Mentor 2026-2027",
      "description": "Peer Mentor 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Peer Mentor 2026-2027 United States | req8505 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Peer Mentor 2026-2027 Summary: The Warrior Peer Mentor Program seeks Peer Mentors for the 2026-2027 academic year. The pay is $13.00/hour which includes all training, and the work as described in the duties above includes assuming the Warrior Welcome Student Leader role during that dedicated period. The work schedule includes a maximum of 10 hours/week during the Fall and Spring semester. Job Summary: A peer mentor is an experienced and thoughtful student leader who is committed to investing one’s time to assist in the growth and development of others. The mentor is willing to share their knowledge, experience, and wisdom and act as a guide and role model. A peer mentor supports and encourages the academic and social development of their mentees and provides active support to help them with adjusting to the ESU/college environment. The peer mentor offers a fresh perspective and an independent point of view, while helping the mentee to succeed. The Peer Mentor program is seeking peer mentors for the 2026-2027 academic year. As a Peer Mentor, you will help guide towards success a group of approximately 50+ new to ESU undergraduate students in your academic program and/or your college during their first year at ESU. This connection begins during Warrior Welcome Weekend and works in tandem with the campus resources throughout the year. The primary mission of the Warrior Peer Mentor Program is to ease the transition of new students to East Stroudsburg University so that they may succeed personally, socially, and academically. Additionally, the program helps each new student (freshmen or transfer) connect with other students, the faculty, student organizations, and staff offering support resources, and ultimately the institution as a whole. The Warrior Peer Mentor Program Objectives: To acquaint each student with East Stroudsburg University—its structure, services, and personalities. To assist the student in personal assessment of his/her abilities and support their transition academically, socially, and personally. To help new students connect with other peers and at least one upper-class student in a meaningful, positive way. To promote class attendance and participation in cultural events. To promote participation in meaningful campus activities. The Warrior Peer Mentor Requirements are: Have and maintain a 2.7 GPA during the time of your appointment. Remain free of disciplinary sanctioning at the suspension level or above. Complete the training modules for the program. General Duties of a Peer Mentor: Acknowledging that each mentoring relationship is unique, the mentor will: Become acquainted with all students in their group and other new students and establish positive relationships. Set positive examples for others in personal, academic, and social behavior. Help build rapport each time he or she meets with a mentee. Ask open-ended “how” and “what” questions with a mentee. Challenge and/or encourage a mentee depending on what the situation requires. Offer opportunities to problem solve and exchange ideas. Provide feedback that is honest, open and positive Take a genuine interest in helping the mentee succeed Present opportunities to the mentee that he/she may not have recognized on his/her own Provide suggestions to the best of one’s knowledge that help the mentee succeed in the program Discuss and monitor the first-year engagement for each of the assigned mentees based on expectations outlined by the Program Director. Schedule, facilitate and prepare summaries of weekly meetings with your group and submit them in a timely manner to the PM Program Director. Maintain individual mentor hours that need to be logged timely. Track attendance for all events and meetings. Contact the Program Director, Dr. Jessica Santiago, immediately should issues arise that the mentor cannot handle. Connect with Student Success Coach in your college for triage on student cases when needed. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8503?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GSW) Graduate Student Worker - Special Education and Rehabilitation Department 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GSW) Graduate Student Worker - Special Education and Rehabilitation Department 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GSW) Graduate Student Worker - Special Education and Rehabilitation Department 2026 - 2027 United States | req8503 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Full-time Graduate Student Worker with the Special Education and Rehabilitation Department working 10-20 hours per week/150-300 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $10.00 per hour Job Summary: Assist faculty with\nspecial projects, NCATE/CAEP/CEC data collection, program brochures, and\ndepartment recruitment materials.  Assist\nin the daily operations of the office and graduate program.  Assist in clerical tasks for department\nfunctioning and/or faculty projects.  Help\nprepare and distribute educational materials to key stakeholders.  Assist in data collection, analysis, and\nreport preparations for research, major accreditation, and other purposes. Responsibilities: Assist in\ndeveloping assessment documents and NCATE/CAEP and CEC reports. Input\nPDE data, assist in aligning assessment documents, assist in developing\nsyllabus templates, and align all materials with NCATE and PDE competency\nrequirements. Assist\nin data collection, analysis, and report preparations/edits and research\nprojects. Assist\nfaculty and staff with campus-wide events and projects, such as Global Week,\nSpecial Olympics, Through Their Eyes, and PPODS Buddy Walk. Assist\nwith all department program documentation, requirements, and responsibilities,\nincluding grant related documentation and program brochures and materials. Utilize\nESU online platforms and assist with other department responsibilities for\nfull-time faculty and adjuncts. Assist\nin preparation of instructional materials for accessibility purposes. Assist\nin the C. R. E. A. T. E. Lab as needed. Use\nof Tk20 and D2L for data collection and instructional support purposes. Assist\nin teacher certification programs at the graduate and undergraduate level.  Assist in the Rehabiltative and Human\nServices program and the Applied Behavior Analyst program. Complete\ngrant related documentation. Assist\nGraduate Coordinator in graduate program activities. Required Qualifications: Enrolled\nfull-time in a Master's Degree program at ESU.  Maintain a 3.0 or higher GPA and no more than one grade below a B.  Ability to maintain confidentiality and\nprofessionalism.  Ability to take\ninitiative, follow directions, and meet deadlines.  Strong written and oral communication\nskills.  Strong technology skills in\nMicrosoft Office software, D2L, email, social media/ networking, and computer applications.  Criminal background checks are required. Preferred\nQualifications: Prefer\ncandidate to be enrolled in the College of Education, although other candidates\nwill be considered. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here:http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8501?c=esu": {
      "title": "Biological Sciences Laboratory Assistant Fall 2026",
      "description": "Biological Sciences Laboratory Assistant Fall 2026 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Biological Sciences Laboratory Assistant Fall 2026 United States | req8501 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Biological Sciences Laboratory Assistant Fall 2026 Job Overview: The laboratory assistant will help with the preparation and set up of labs for the Introductory Biology 1 and Microbiology courses as well as more general tasks such as cleaning and stocking the prep lab and maintaining inventory. Some of the skills you will learn through this position are listed below. No previous experience is required. There are also ample opportunities for students to pursue areas of interest or focus on a specific skill set they may be interested in. Anticipated start date: 08/24/2026 Anticipated end date: 12/12/2026 Hourly rate: $9 Hours per week: 10-20 Location: Moore Biology Hall room 114 Responsibilities: General lab safety and good laboratory practices. Assist with preparing chemical solutions, safe chemical handling, storage and disposal. Assist with preparing microbiology media including broths, agar plates and agar tubes. Equipment use, maintenance and some repair, including microscopes, water baths, pH meters, scales, spectrophotometers and gas sensors. Assist with aquaria care for several freshwater planted tanks. Monitoring plant and animal health, water quality and troubleshooting issues that may arise. Assist with greenhouse care, repotting and fertilizing plants as necessary, propagation of plants, monitoring and treating disease and/or pests as well as watering. Assist with maintaining general and chemical inventory using our inventory database LabArchives. Qualifications: Must be a student within the biological sciences department. No other previous experience necessary, any class level accepted. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8500?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletic Training Department 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletic Training Department 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletic Training Department 2026 - 2027 United States | req8500 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant with the Athletic Training Department working 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: Assist Dept. of Athletics Athletic training Staff with prevention, recognition, assessment and immediate care of athletic injuries Assist with Athletic Rehabilitations Assist with Preparation Screenings Educate athletes, coaches and athletic training students on injury Attend and provide emergency care coverage as assigned by the coordinator of athletic training services Conduct injury assessment and injury referral as needed Maintain adequate and proper record keeping including: Inputting medical records into the Sports-Related Data Base Filling all medical paperwork Assist with general maintenance of the athletic training room Required Qualifications: Admission to East Stroudsburg University. Graduate school application may occur at the same time as applying for the position. A Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. Criminal background check Ability to work nights and weekends Computer competency Driver’s license Excellent communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Professional interest in pursuing a career in intercollegiate athletics. Ability to take initiative and ownership of special events Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
