    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8493?c=esu": {
      "title": "Reptile Animal Care Student Worker Fall 2026-Spring 2027",
      "description": "Reptile Animal Care Student Worker Fall 2026-Spring 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Reptile Animal Care Student Worker Fall 2026-Spring 2027 United States | req8493 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Reptile Animal Care Student Worker Fall 2026-Spring 2027 Job Overview: The Biology Department seeks a dedicated and detail-oriented student worker to work together with other students and professors to\nadminister the best possible care to the animals housed at East Stroudsburg\nUniversity.  These animals include\ninvertebrates, fish, amphibians, reptiles, and rodents. Anticipated start date: 08/24/2026 Anticipated end date: 5/15/2027 Hourly rate: $9 Hours per week: 10 Duties and Responsibilities: Become\nfamiliar with approved Standard Operating Procedures related to animal care. Complete\nweb-based training modules on the proper care and housing of laboratory animals\nprovided   through the American Association of Laboratory Animal Sciences. Assist in\ncarrying out daily check-ins of animal care facilities Keep facilities clean and in accordance with USDA guidelines Learn how\nto operate cage washer Work\ntogether as a part of a team to ensure optimal health of animals under your\ncare by providing a clean environment and optimal nutrition for those animals Keep\nrecords of animal care up to date and report on the health of the animals\nregularly Work with\nthe IACUC veterinarian to assure that any treatment protocols of sick or\ninjured animals are carried out properly Qualifications: Must be a student within the biological sciences department. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8492?c=esu": {
      "title": "Facilities Front Office Student Worker",
      "description": "Facilities Front Office Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Facilities Front Office Student Worker United States | req8492 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Facilities Front Office Student Worker Job Summary: The Front Office Student Worker will assist with the administrative functions of\nFacilities Management. This role involves handling customer inquiries, service\nrequests, and assisting with campus facility records under the supervision of\noffice staff. Job Duties: Answer phones, assist visitors, and respond to general inquiries at the service call desk. Receive, log, and process routine and emergency work requests; escalate urgent issues to the clerical staff, Customer Care Manager or relevant trades. Perform data entry, filing, scanning, and\ndigital record-keeping. Assist with key requests, electronic access updates, and ESU Fleet vehicle coordination. Support staff in surveying building spaces, updating campus directories, and performing supervised ADA compliance checks. Complete other clerical tasks and related duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Current ESU Student Ability to lift, pull, and push up to 40lbs. Basic computer skills. Experience in customer service. Ability to skillfully complete clerical work. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $15.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8491?c=esu": {
      "title": "Facilities Mailroom and Warehouse Student Worker",
      "description": "Facilities Mailroom and Warehouse Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Facilities Mailroom and Warehouse Student Worker United States | req8491 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Facilities Mailroom and Warehouse Student Worker Job Summary: This role will be supporting the facilities management mailroom and receiving & distribution center. Warehouse Job Duties: Receives, unpacks, checks, and records the receipt of goods. Stores goods in proper storage places. Receives delivery orders. Withdraw goods from stock. Checking for required commodity, size, and lot. Receives signed delivery ticket. Assist with assembling stock items in accordance with a computerized requisition. Assist with packing shipments and loading goods. Mailroom Job Duties: Assist with Delivery of mail stops at University Departments. Assist full time clerks with large mailings: non-automated presort standard, nonprofit, and periodicals. Return and sort mail for university offices. Do tabbing for both automated and non-automated mailings. Assist in the redirection of mail for students who have move to another room or off campus. Assist in the Picking up of packages or envelopes. Act as messenger when required to pick up package or envelopes from campus departments. Job Requirements: Current ESU Student Ability to lift, pull, and push up to 40lbs. Basic computer skills. Experience in customer service. Ability to skillfully complete clerical work. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $15.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8489?c=esu": {
      "title": "Student Wildlife Field Technician",
      "description": "Student Wildlife Field Technician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student Wildlife Field Technician United States | req8489 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Student Wildlife Field Technician Job Summary: The Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife Genetics Institute is seeking student\nworkers to assist with our field research and sample collections. Field\nresearch will include trapping and sampling small mammals, and conducting tick\ndrags to collect ticks. This position will also include laboratory time to document\nand store samples following SOP, and identification of ticks collected. This is\na unique opportunity to support research on vector borne disease. The candidate will perform a variety of functions in support\nof the research group. Primary duties will involve projects that are focused on\nfield research for collection of ticks, identifying and storing ticks by\ncollection site. Hours : up to 20 hours per week Pay : $12.00 per hour Responsibilities: Adherence to laboratory and field safety procedures and Standards of Practice are essential. Assist Field Technicians with trapping and sampling small mammals following IACUC protocols and the laboratories research methods. Assist Field Technicians with tick drags to collect, identify and store samples. Document all activities using electronic laboratory information system. Input data into computer programs. Assist with GIS mapping. Learn how to analye and interpret data. Requirements: Successful candidates will be self-motivated, organized, independent, and eager to learn a breadth of techniques. Occasional evening and/or weekend work will be required. Ability to walk and hike through various terrains and work in various temperatures. Must have excellent critical thinking, problem solving, verbal and written skills, deductive reasoning and highly perceptive and detail oriented. Successful candidate must work well in small and large groups. Registered student pursuing a bachelors or graduate degree in Biological sciences, or related degree, with an overall GPA of 3.0 or higher. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8478?c=esu": {
      "title": "Director of Student Accounts",
      "description": "Director of Student Accounts | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Student Accounts United States | req8478 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Director of Student Accounts, you will need to skillfully execute the coordination of student billing to assist with the collection process along with flawlessly allocating the correct amount of funds to student accounts. You will be an active member of the Business Office team and will work closely with the Chief Financial Officer serving as support for the financial health of the institution by innovating procedures centered on efficient operations to positively impact the customer experience. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your business background and extensive student accounts experience all while tactfully leading your team to provide comprehensive counseling students & their families on resources offered to them. To be successful in this role, you must demonstrate an excellent level of detail, possess strong supervisory skills, and be able to manage complex processes in a student-centered and compliance-driven environment. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Director of Student Accounts.  When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Oversee the collection of outstanding student\nbalances, document clear procedures, and collaborate with Administration and\nFinance to develop strategies and metrics to reduce student receivables. Ensures that federal, state, and other\nreporting requirements are timely, including the A133 audit, FISAP, and other\nmandatory filings. Develop and maintain a Student Accounts procedural manual that supports fiscal\ncontrols and compliance with university funding directives. Identify and\nimplement more efficient processes and procedures in accordance with U.S.\nDepartment of Education, PASSHE, ESU, and NACUBO standards. Develop materials and conduct presentations\nand workshops that educate students on financial literacy and responsibility. Manage the Accounts Receivable module of the\nstudent information system. Act as systems administrator for the online\npayment gateway ancillary system. Work with enrollment systems manager on\nrolling out module enhancements and system updates. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Bachelor's\ndegree in business-related field; Master’s degree preferred. Five or more years experience in Student Accounts with\nextensive knowledge of Title IV cash management regulations and administering\nfederal and state aid programs. Demonstrated experience with providing\nprojections for 1-2 years for budgeting. Minimum of 3 years supervising staff in a\nhighly controlled environment. Working in a union environment helpful. Experience-using Banner, PeopleSoft or another\nmajor student information system helpful. Possess the polished ability to pivot between tasks that may interrupt handling detail-oriented work. Demonstrate the ability to navigate time constraints\nand communicate updates in a deadline-oriented environment. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: Based on Experience Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8477?c=esu": {
      "title": "Residence Life & Housing Student Desk Worker 2026-2027",
      "description": "Residence Life & Housing Student Desk Worker 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Residence Life & Housing Student Desk Worker 2026-2027 United States | req8477 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Residence Life & Housing Student Desk Worker 2026-2027 Academic Year Student Desk\nWorker Overview: Student Desk Workers (SDW’s) are one tier of our security structure and first impressions of our Resident Halls. As a team member of the Office of Residential Life and Housing, SDW’s are an integral part of daily Residential Life Operations and overall experience for residents in our communities. Student Desk\nWorker Expectations: SDW’s are expected to arrive on time for all scheduled and assigned shifts. SDW’s are expected to stay for entire scheduled shifts. SDW’s are expected to find appropriate coverage for shifts they become unavailable to work. SDW’s are expected to actively participate in all training workshops and in-service programs. Student Desk\nWorker Qualifications: SDW’s must stay in good academic standing by maintaining a minimum overall Grade Point Average (GPA) of 2.2 or higher during employment. SDW’s must stay in good conduct standing with The University by not being on a sanction status or higher during employment. Student Desk\nWorker Permitted Hours: SDW’s are eligible to work up to 20 hours per week in accordance with ESU Regulations. Compensation : Hourly Rate\nfor Pay at $9.00 Student Desk\nWorker Employee Timelines: Fall 2026: Fall 2026 Move-In: SDW’s will be expected to move-in on Thursday, August 13th, 2026, by 4:00 p.m. SDW’s training will begin on this date and continue through the weekend of Friday, August 14th and Monday, August 17th, 2026. SDW’s will hold no other commitments through Sunday, August 23rd, 2026, to assist with move-in week and start of semester operations. August 18th-23rd, 2026 - Residence Halls Move-In Occurs for the Fall 2026 Semester. Labor Day/ Weekend 2026: SDW’s operations will operate as normal on the Weekend and Monday of the Labor Day Holiday in the Resident Halls. The ESU Resident Halls are not closed during this holiday. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. Indigenous People’s Weekend 2026: SDW’s operations will operate as normal on the Weekend and Monday of the Indigenous People’s Holiday in the Resident Halls.The ESU Resident Halls are not closed during this holiday. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. Fall Break 2026: SDW’s operations will operate as normal on Fall Break. The ESU Resident Halls are not closed during this time period. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. Thanksgiving Break 2026: SDW’s will have Resident Hall Desk Operations until Tuesday, November 24, 2026, at 12/Midnight. Residence Halls Close at 12/ Noon on Wednesday, November 25th, 2026. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. SDW’s will resume Resident Hall Desk Operations on Sunday, November 29, 2026. Residence Halls Open at 12:00 /Noon from Break. SDWs who are scheduled to work are required to return by start of scheduled shift, if scheduled for shift this date. Winter Break: SDW’s will have Resident Hall Desk Operations until Friday, December 11th, 2026 at 12/Midnight. Residence Halls Close at 12:00/Noon on Saturday, December 12th, 2026 for Break. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for shifts. SDW’s are required to operate adjusted schedules during Finals Week 2026 in relation to their exams schedule. Spring 2027: Spring 2027 Move-In: SDW’s will be expected to move in on Friday, January 15th, 2027, by 4:00 p.m. SDW’s operations will begin on this date and continue through the weekend until the first day of classes for the Spring 2027 semester. Marin Luther King Jr. (MLK) Day\n2027: SDW’s operations will operate as normal on this Monday in the resident halls.The ESU Resident Halls are not closed during this holiday. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. Spring Break 2027: SDW’s will have Resident Hall Desk Operations until Friday, March 5th, 2027, at 12/Midnight. SDWs are required to stay and work, if scheduled for their routine shift. Residence Halls Close at 12/ Noon on Saturday, Friday, March 6th, 2027. SDW’s will resume Resident Hall Desk Operations on Sunday, March 14th, 2027. Residence Halls Open at 12:00/Noon from Break. SDWs who are scheduled to work are required to return by start of scheduled shift, if scheduled for shift this date. Spring Move-Out: SDW’s will have Resident Hall Desk Operations until Saturday, May 8th, 2027. Residence Halls Close at 12/Noon on Sunday, May 9th for Summer 2027. SDWs are required to stay and work if scheduled for routine shifts. SDW’s are required to operate adjusted schedules during Finals Week Spring 2027 in relation to their exams schedule. **NOTE: Dates and Times listed are subject to\nchange during Summer 2026 for Fall 2026 and during Fall 2026 for Spring 2027. SDW General\nResponsibilities: SDW’s are expected to enforce and affirm that all residents and guests swipe into respective resident halls each time entering a resident hall. Be available to assist in all openings and all closings of your assigned residence hall as listed above in the Employment Timeline for the 2026-2027 Academic Year. SDW’s will file a Duty Log for all shifts worked for the Office of Residential Life and Housing to document events of shifts. Build a good working relationship with your immediate assigned resident hall team and building members. Provide excellent customer service to all residents and guests of the building. Actively and regularly communicate with Supervisor, Assistant Director of Residential Life Actively and regularly communicate with Pro Staff of assigned resident hall. Actively and regularly fellow staff members using multiple means (electronic and in person) as defined by your supervisor(s). Serve as a role model for residents. Connect with Resident Directors/Supervisor for any support needed in all aspects of the role. Attend staff meetings and meet individually with Pro Staff of assigned resident hall as requested. Assist in the training of new staff members as requested. Read and implement staff announcements and directives. Enforce and report University policies and procedures. Fulfill assigned clerical duties while at the desk (ex: answer telephone/take message, refer package requests to central office. Serve as a resource and referral person of university operations and the functions of the various University administrative offices. Recognize and fulfill your responsibilities with evacuation drills and other emergency situations. Respect individual privacy and the confidential nature of information about individual students per guidelines from the Office of Residential Life and Housing. Comply with and enforce all Federal, State and Local Laws and all University regulations. **PLEASE NOTE: Responsibilities are subject to change. Additional Information: By submitting an application, I authorize the Residential\nLife and Housing Office to review my student conduct and academic file in\nrelation to my application to the Student Desk Worker Position. Further, I acknowledge that the information contained in this\napplication is accurate to the best of my knowledge. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8469?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Academic Affairs 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Academic Affairs 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Academic Affairs 2026 - 2027 United States | req8469 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant working in the Academic Affairs department 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Description: Assist the Assistant to the Provost in day-to-day operational duties in the Office of the Provost. Participate in special projects to support academic affairs programs. Attend periodic meetings and take minutes for meetings as approved by the Provost/Assistant to the Provost. Assist with Academic Affairs budget procedures with the Assistant to the Provost including processing requests, travel approval and expense forms, etc. Assist in office duties such as answering telephones, filing and data entry. Other duties as assigned. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8449?c=esu": {
      "title": "Peer Tutor 26-27",
      "description": "Peer Tutor 26-27 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Peer Tutor 26-27 United States | req8449 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The University Wide Tutoring Program is searching for Students to Become Peer Tutors Job Summary: Tutors are assigned to 100 and 200 level general education courses and some upper division courses with historically high failure rates. Tutors assist students who have various levels of knowledge gain a clearer and a deeper understanding of a particular subject in a collaborative and active learning environment.  Tutors are responsible for tutoring students in individual, drop-in, appointment-based or group sessions in a particular subject area.  All tutors must attend College of Reading and Learning Association (CRLA) tutor training workshops and meetings required by the Tutoring Center Director and/or Coordinator and fulfill other responsibilities related to tutoring.  Hours and types of tutoring will be determined in coordination with the Tutoring Center Director and/or Coordinator. Tutor responsibilities include: Tutor students in individual, appointment-based and/or drop-in tutoring sessions. Know the syllabi, assignments and requirements of courses tutoring. Enforce WTC and MathQC policies. Attend and contribute to tutor team meetings throughout the semester. Be available to tutor up to twenty hours of drop-in lab time during WTC hours. Meet with each class for which you tutor at least two times a semester. Meet with professor for each class you tutor at least two times a semester. Be available to schedule one-on-one, 30-60 minute weekly tutoring sessions. Attend College of Reading and Learning Association (CRLA) staff training workshops. Commit to a semester long work experience. Required Qualifications to become a Tutor: Maintain a 3.0 Cumulative GPA. Be a second year (sophomore) undergraduate student at East Stroudsburg University. Have a final grade of \"A\" or \"B\" in the course(s) you wish to tutor. Preferred Qualifications to Become a Tutor: Demonstrate the ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Demonstrate the ability to promote a positive work environment. Demonstrate the ability to work with minimal supervision and to initiate work on projects independently. Demonstrate knowledge in the appropriate disciplines. Have the ability to work well with others. Pay Rate: $12.00 per hour Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8448?c=esu": {
      "title": "Learning Assistant for Supplemental Instruction 2026-27",
      "description": "Learning Assistant for Supplemental Instruction 2026-27 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Learning Assistant for Supplemental Instruction 2026-27 United States | req8448 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Learning Assistants for Supplemental Instruction Job Summary: LAs help students who have various\nlevels of knowledge gain a clearer and a deeper understanding of a particular\nsubject in a collaborative and active learning environment. LAs workup to 11 hours per week. Specific times and day are determined in coordination with the\nprofessor for the course and the Tutorial Director & Coordinator. Pay rate: $13.00 per hour. LA responsibilities include: Hold weekly review and discussion sessions Have a thorough understanding of the syllabi, assignments and requirements for the courses. Attend the course with the students. Assist the professor with course related duties in and out of class (up to three hours\noutside of class each week). Prepare and submitweekly session plans. Enforce UWTP policies. Attend and contribute to LA team meetings throughout the semester. Be availableto tutor up to two hours duringWTC hours. Meet with professor as needed. Attend mandatory LA training workshops. Commit to a semester long work experience. Required Qualifications: 1. Submit a recommendation from the professor who teaches the course. 2. Successfully complete an interview with the Tutorial Coordinator. 3. Maintain a 3.0 Cumulative GPA. 4. Be a second year (sophomore) undergraduate student at East Stroudsburg University. 5. Have a final grade of \"A,\" “A-,“ “B+,” or \"B\" in the course(s). Preferred Qualifications: 1. Demonstrate the ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, and staff. 2. Demonstrate the ability to promote a positive work environment. 3. Demonstrate the ability to work with minimal supervision and to initiate work on projects independently. 4. Demonstrate knowledge in the appropriate disciplines. 5. Have the Ability to work well with others. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8421?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics/Athletic Training 2026 - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics/Athletic Training 2026 - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Athletics/Athletic Training 2026 - 2027 United States | req8421 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant with the Athletic Training department working 20 hours per week/300 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Responsibilities: Engage in the prevention, recognition, assessment and immediate care of\nathletic injuries. Integrates the graduate assistantship experiences with their academic\ncourse work in Athletic Training. Support teaching and research agenda of the Athletic Training Department. Communicates confidentially with supervisors regarding injury status and\nhealth conditions. Attends and provides emergency care coverage for assigned events. Conducts injury assessments as needed to determine referral needs. Performs administrative duties including EAPs, SOPs and maintaining\nvarious injury and/or treatment logs/reports. Educate athletes, patients/clients and coaches on injury prevention and\nstatus. Required Qualifications: Eligible for BOC® Certification as an Athletic Trainer Temporary or Permanent Pennsylvania Certification as an Athletic Trainer Current Professional Rescuer CPR, AED and FIRST AID Required:  Act 34 (PA Criminal\nBackground Clearance) Required:  Act 114 (FBI Criminal\nBackground Clearance: Fingerprinting) Required:  Act 151 (Child Abuse\nHistory Clearance) Required:  Professional Liability Insurance Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8414?c=esu": {
      "title": "Campus Rec & Wellness Attendant 2026-2027",
      "description": "Campus Rec & Wellness Attendant 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Campus Rec & Wellness Attendant 2026-2027 United States | req8414 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search ESU Campus Rec & Wellness Recreation Center Attendant 2026 to 2027 The Recreation Attendant will perform general duties as well\nas membership service desk and/or the fitness center duties.  The position will report to the Facility\nManager (shift supervisor). Responsibilities: Implement facility rules and\nregulations in all areas of the Mattioli Recreation Center and RecB. Ensure\nthe cleanliness and maintenance of the facility and machines. Promote\nCampus Rec & Wellness programs. Answer\nphone calls in a friendly and professional manner, transfer calls and take\nmessages as required. Provide prompt,\nfriendly, and professional answers to questions posed by our customers. Find\ncoverage for any assigned shift that you may not be able to work. Provide\nfirst aid when necessary. Ability\nto learn how to set-up and break-down of equipment used in the Recreation\nCenter. Must\nbe available for morning, late night, and weekend shifts including breaks and\nholidays. Wear appropriate attire (including staff\nshirts) for all shifts. Fulfill\nother duties as assigned by the Facility Manager, Graduate Assistant, Assistant\nDirector of Campus Rec & Wellness, Director of Campus Rec & Wellness, or\nthe Executive Director of the Student Activity Association, Inc. Service Desk responsibilities: Follow the equipment check-out/return policy Oversee all reservations and drop-in play Provide facility tours for new users Assist with membership questions, money collection or\n      transactions. Fitness\nCenter responsibilities: Provide a spot for persons lifting when necessary Ensure members are re-racking weights and wiping down\n      machines Keep the Fitness Center’s equipment and accessories\n      neat, organized, and clean Perform daily and monthly cleaning duties of all\n      equipment Qualifications: First Aid, CPR\n     and AED certifications. Be in good\n     standing according to ESU’s Student Code of Conduct. Enrolled as an\n     ESU student. Required to\n     complete the mandatory Title IX, Cleary Act, and Pennsylvania Minors\n     Clearances as well as background checks and fingerprints prior to\n     beginning.' Preferred Qualifications: Dependable\nand punctual. Ability\nto work with people and follow directions. May\nrequire heavy lifting (of over 50lbs) and climbing ladders. Must be\nwilling to perform custodial/maintenance duties. Additional Information: ESU\nRecreation Attendants are paid $10.00 an hour, for between 8-15 hours per week. Evaluations\nwill be completed with end of semester review through one-on-one discussions. Role will start August 2026 with the potential to start before based on need. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
