    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8393?c=esu": {
      "title": "Human Anatomy & Physiology Student Worker",
      "description": "Human Anatomy & Physiology Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Human Anatomy & Physiology Student Worker United States | req8393 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Human Anatomy & Physiology Student Worker Job Summary: East Stroudsburg University’s Biological Sciences Dept. seeks a student to provide assistance for Biology department. The student worker will attend the weekly sessions and assist the professor in prepping/cleaning up after class. Additionally, the student worker will help organize supplies. Duties: Assist Dr. Kavanau with preparing instructional materials for Human Anatomy\n& Physiology for the Health Sciences and Biology laboratory courses. Assisting in organizing worksheets, PowerPoint\npresentations, study guides, and other student support resources, Assisting with laboratory materials and supporting student recognition efforts The student worker will attend the weekly sessions and assist the professor in prepping/cleaning up after class. Qualifications: Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and professionalism are required. Current ESU Student. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $8.50 10 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8378?c=esu": {
      "title": "Temporary Research Technician",
      "description": "Temporary Research Technician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temporary Research Technician United States | req8378 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Temporary Research Technician, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable conducting advanced scientific experimentation to evaluate various environmental and biological sample types. You will be an active member of the Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife Genetics Institute team and will work closely with the Director to skillfully perform test procedures in search of pathogens from specimens. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your biology or veterinary background and professional laboratory experience all while utilizing various apparatuses to execute DNA/RNA procedures or polymerase chain reactions. To be successful in this role the applicant must be eager to learn a breadth of techniques, strong critical thinking and communication skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule to work evenings or weekends from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Temporary Research Technician. This role requires up to 10% travel.  When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Maintaining successful completion of proficiency testing in aseptic techniques, DNA/RNA extractions, and PCR. Performs laboratory testing using scientific techniques, such as DNA/RNA extractions, and polymerase chain reaction (PCR) to determine the presence, or absence of bacterial, protozoa, fungi, viruses, or other pathogenic microorganisms. Performs laboratory testing using scientific techniques such as genotyping, and genetic sequencing to evaluate genotypes, strain, and haplotype differences of pathogens or wildlife populations. Maintains data using electronic recording and documentation of sample processing based on approved standards of practice. Conducts required quality assurance and quality control procedures to ensure reagents, media, apparatus, and processes meet required performance standards. Assists with generating scientific protocols to be used in research conducted within the laboratory and assist Research Assistant with projects on tick-borne illnesses or population genetics. Identify various ticks to species and life stages and ability to use dichotomous keys to identify unknown specimens. Maintains, cleans, and calibrates all scientific equipment based on manufacturers and laboratory standards of practice. Updates and maintains current standards of practice and inventory logs and processes. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Associates degree in Veterinary Laboratory Technology (VLT) or Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) and one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory. Or Two years of college which includes six (6) credits in biology, three (3) credits in chemistry, and three (3) credits in microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, histology or biostatistics and one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory. Or An equivalent combination of experience and training which included one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory, and six (6) college credits in biology, three (3) college credits in chemistry, and three (3) college credits in microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, histology or biostatistics. One year of experience work in a research laboratory or one-year technical laboratory experience or any equivalent combination of experience and training. A Bachelor’s degree of Science in Microbiology, Biology, Biotechnology, or a related field with a minimum of 20 credit hours in Genetics, Molecular Biology, Biotechnology, Microbiology, Cellular Biology, and Biochemistry preferred. Minimum of 1-year experience working in a molecular, biotechnology or similar laboratory preferred. One-year experience with sample handling, DNA extractions, and Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is preferred. One-year experience identifying ticks and knowledge on ticks and tick-borne diseases in Pennsylvania is preferred. Strong communication skills to efficiently with lead laboratory staff on experimentations and laboratory processes. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $1,795.50 biweekly Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8373?c=esu": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker 1",
      "description": "Custodial Worker 1 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Custodial Worker 1 United States | req8373 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Custodial Worker 1, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable completing routine custodial care for the University Buildings and surrounding grounds. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Manager of Building Care Services to help achieve consistent building care for ESU. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your custodial and maintenance experience while safely using cleaning products to sanitize the buildings and surrounding area. To be successful in this role, you must be self-motivated, detail-oriented, and have time management skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 11:00 PM to 07:00 AM. You may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Custodial Worker 1. Indoor work is 90% of the role with 10% of the role occasionally completed outside in the snow and or rain. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Sweeps, mops, vacuums, scrubs, waxes, and buffs floors. Cleans, dusts, and polishes furniture and fixtures. Washes and cleans windows, walls, and doors. Cleans toilets, sinks, and mirrors in restrooms and replaces restroom supplies. Utilizes tools and equipment of the custodial trade in the performance of cleaning tasks. Gathers and disposes of waste products, recyclable materials, infectious waste, and hazardous materials according to safe material handling guidelines. Moves furniture and equipment when necessary to perform custodial tasks. Secures and maintains cleaning equipment; requests, picks up, and stores related supplies. Reports needed repairs to crew leader or supervisor. Shovels snow, sweeps and cleans walks, and assists in keeping immediate outside premises and building entrances in an orderly condition. Performs incidental assignments, such as removing ashes, replacing lightbulbs, and making simple repairs. Documents work performed. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Able to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Able to lift, push, pull, or carry 50lbs. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: 32,724 annually Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8368?c=esu": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "Student Office Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student Office Assistant United States | req8368 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search ESU's Business Accelerator and Entrepreneurship Program is searching for a Student Office Assistant Purpose: The student will assist the Business Accelerator/Entrepreneurship\nPrograms, J-1 VISA, Pocono Mountains Keystone Innovation Zone, with activities,\nprograms, competitions community outreach, marketing, and data collection\nanalysis. Responsibilities: Assist\nin the planning, preparation, and management of Business Accelerator events and\nprograms such as the ESU Warrior Startup Challenge, and Entrepreneurship Club. Communicate\nand collaborate with other ESU departments, staff, faculty, and external\nclients to advance the goals and mission of the Business Accelerator. Perform\noffice functions including but not limited to, delivering mail, submitting work\norders, answering phones, and helping other staff and offices as needed. Qualifications: Current ESU Student. All Majors are welcomed. Organizational\nskills with the ability to work on multiple projects concurrently. Ability\nto think critically and creatively. Ability\nto follow instructions, communicate, and work both independently and as part of\na team. Professional\nwriting and communication skills Fluent\nusing Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint, Canva and Adobe Additional Information: Hourly Rate $15.00 Up to 10 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8365?c=esu": {
      "title": "Reading Student Worker",
      "description": "Reading Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Reading Student Worker United States | req8365 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Reading Department is searching for Student Workers Job Summary/Basic Function: Must Greet and support students, campus visitors and\n     other professionals with department resources. Must be proficient in the use\n     of Office Windows-Word, Excel, Power Point, etc. Should have excellent communication\n     skills, written and verbal, be able to answer phones and take messages\n     when necessary. Handle and deliver mail received by the office daily. Make copies as requested by\n     professors. Assist professors with any special events as requested. Maintain a high quality of\n     professionalism and ethical behavior. Perform other duties as assigned by the department chair\n     and Secretary. Job Requirements: Currently enrolled\n     undergraduate student at East Stroudsburg University. Must be professional,\n     organized, and dependable with a high degree of integrity. Report to work as scheduled,\n     complete assignments, respond to communication quickly. Must have a positive attitude\n     and be courteous with excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must speak clearly on the\n     phone, with a positive, upbeat, and courteous attitude. Ability to communicate and work\n     well with a diverse staff and other student. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $10.00 Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
