    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8342?c=esu": {
      "title": "Writing Studio Tutor 2026-2027",
      "description": "Writing Studio Tutor 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Writing Studio Tutor 2026-2027 United States | req8342 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Writing Studio is Looking for a Motivated Studio Tutor Experienced tutors returning to the Writing Studio will help ESU students learn new strategies for improving their writing. Tutors work with students one-to-one or in small groups, help mentor new tutors, and may visit classes to provide tips on writing. Tutors will work a set schedule throughout each semester and will participate in training and development activities to foster their own professional growth. Responsibilities: Help ESU students learn new strategies for improving their writing. Work with students one-to-one, providing feedback and help for writing projects. Work set schedule throughout each semester and will participate in training and development activities to foster their own professional growth and help to mentor new tutors. Qualifications: Solid writing skills. Good communication skills. Ability to work and interact well with others on a team Must have a 3.0 GPA. Pay Rate: $12 - 14.00 Hourly Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8332?c=esu": {
      "title": "Transfer Admission Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Transfer Admission Student Ambassador | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Transfer Admission Student Ambassador United States | req8332 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Transfer Admission Student Ambassador Position Summary: Transfer Center Admission Ambassador are responsible for welcoming prospective students and families to ESU. Transfer Center Admission Ambassadors will work with the office supporting the transfer center staff to prepare and set up Admission events, lead campus tours, and help prospective students navigate their college journey. Responsibilities: Lead and guide prospective transfer and nontraditional students and families on campus tours and identify important campus locations. Address concerns and questions from prospective transfer and nontraditional students and their families. Be available to support various admission and transfer events, which may include weekend programs and campus visit activities. Share personal ESU experiences with prospective students and families. Connect families with the Transfer Center staff. Prepare event materials, make event folders, and participate in event logistics. Qualifications: Be enrolled at ESU as a full-time student. Maintain a 2.50 cumulative and semester GPA . Be in good academic and judicial standing. Display high levels of professionalism when representing ESU. Work well in group settings and with individuals. Must be available for all of the Admission Events. Open Houses: April 11th and April 25th. Weekend Visit:  February 28th. Be a good public speaker. Be knowledgeable about ESU campus, events, and student experience. Additional Information: Hourly rate $12.00 to $15.00. Up to 20 hours per week (subject to change) Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8301?c=esu": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice United States | req8301 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The successful candidate\nwill join a cohesive, collaborative and diverse multidisciplinary department that\noffers majors and minors in Criminal Justice, Sociology, and Social Work. The\nCriminal Justice program offers a comprehensive foundation of core courses, in\naddition to a wide variety of elective courses and opportunities for\ninternships and experiential learning. Applicants must possess prior\nuniversity-level teaching experience, and be able to teach both introductory\nsurvey courses, and upper-level major electives in an area of expertise. While\nall specialty areas will be considered, preference will be given to candidates\nwho: Demonstrate a strong background teaching courses related to the Courts/Judicial Process (to include\nareas such as bail, plea-bargaining, the trial & sentencing for example); OR topics of Social Inequalities, Crime and\nJustice (to include areas such as racial and ethnic disparities in crime\nand criminal justice, women in criminal justice, poverty and crime for\nexample); AND an open secondary area of specialization in teaching and/or\nresearch. The successful candidate\nwill have a 4/4 teaching load and is also expected to maintain a focused\nscholarly agenda and provide service to the Department and University. The\nposition also requires working with other department faculty in developing\nprogramming activities and events, as well as culturally responsive curriculum\nand pedagogy. Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Criminal Justice, Criminology or closely related\nprogram of study (ABD considered provided dissertation defense date guarantees\nconferral of degree before date of appointment). Experience teaching Criminal Justice and/or closely related\nsubject(s) at the post-secondary level. Evidence of ongoing scholarly activity. Minimum of two (2) years professional experience in Criminal\nJustice or closely related field. The ability to work with diverse populations. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Family Tuition waivers: Every full-time employee will receive a full tuition waiver\nfor all ESU courses for themselves, spouse/domestic partner, and children.  Every full-time employee will receive 50%\ntuition waiver at all PASSHE universities for themselves, spouse/domestic\npartner, and children. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and must include: (1) a cover letter, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of your teaching philosophy, (4) a research plan involving undergraduate, (5) a statement on your approach to inclusive teaching of a diverse student population and (6) unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts. Additional materials, including official transcripts and three letters of reference, will be requested from finalists. ABD candidates must provide authoritative documentation supporting Ph.D. conferral date. Only completed applications will receive consideration. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8295?c=esu": {
      "title": "Art+ Media+ Design Studio Monitor",
      "description": "Art+ Media+ Design Studio Monitor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Art+ Media+ Design Studio Monitor United States | req8295 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Art + Media + Design Department is Searching for a Studio Monitor Job Summary: The Art + Media + Design Department is seeking a\nstudent Art + Media + Design Major to be a studio monitor. Students must\nbe responsible and willing to help with multiple tasks in both the 3D Printing and Product Design Studio. Monitors will make sure the G2 lab is open to\nstudents taking Art + Media + Design classes during their designated time slots\nand enforce studio rules during open hours. They will be responsible for\nproperly shutting down and locking the lab once their time slot is finished. Monitors will help professors process files and\nproduce digital fabrications on 3d printers, laser-cutting and CNC equipment during\nsemester. Monitors will help clean the labs and organize\nfacilities per faculty’s request. They are also responsible for general\ncomputer maintenance on the both studios’ laptops. Additional Information: 8-15 hrs. a week subject to change Hourly rate $10.00 Must be a current ESU Student Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8285?c=esu": {
      "title": "Facilities Management Student Assistant",
      "description": "Facilities Management Student Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Facilities Management Student Assistant United States | req8285 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Facilities Management Student Assistant Job Summary: This role will be supporting the facilities management mailroom and receiving & distribution center. Warehouse Job Duties: Receives, unpacks, checks, and records the receipt of goods. Stores goods in proper storage places. Receives delivery orders. Withdraw goods from stock. Checking for required commodity, size, and lot. Receives signed delivery ticket. Assist with assembling stock items in accordance with a computerized requisition. Assist with packing shipments and loading goods. Mailroom Job Duties: Assist with Delivery of\n     mail stops at University Departments. Assist full time clerks\n     with large mailings: non-automated presort standard, nonprofit, and\n     periodicals. Return and sort mail for university offices. Do tabbing for both\n     automated and non-automated mailings. Assist in the redirection\n     of mail for students who have move to another room or off campus. Assist in the Picking\n     up of packages or envelopes. Act as messenger when\n     required to pick up package or envelopes from campus departments. Job Requirements: Current ESU Student Ability to lift, pull, and push up to 40lbs. Basic computer skills. experience in customer service. Ability to skillfully complete clerical work. Additional Information: Hourly Rate $15.00 Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8284?c=esu": {
      "title": "Health Studies Office Aide",
      "description": "Health Studies Office Aide | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Health Studies Office Aide United States | req8284 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Health Studies Office Aide Job Responsibilities: Assist faculty member with requests. Assist departmental day to day operations to maintain function. Greet and assist incoming customers. Support the departments secretary with various office tasks such as answering phones, making copies of documents, filing paperwork, and completing errands. Qualifications: Current ESU Student. Ability to communicate effectively with customers to best assist them. Additional Information: Hourly Rate is $8.00. Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
