    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8263?c=esu": {
      "title": "Marine Science Aquatic Care Student Worker",
      "description": "Marine Science Aquatic Care Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Marine Science Aquatic Care Student Worker United States | req8263 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Marine Science Aquatic\nCare Student Worker Job Summary: To work together with other students and professors to administer the best possible care to the animals housed at East Stroudsburg University.  These animals include invertebrates, fish, amphibians, reptiles, and rodents. Key Responsibilities: Become familiar with approved Standard Operating Procedures related to animal care. Complete web-based training modules on the proper care and housing of laboratory animals provided through the American Association of Laboratory Animal Sciences. Assist in carrying out daily check-ins of animal care facilities. Keep facilities clean and in accordance with USDA guidelines. Learn how to operate cage washer. Work together as a part of a team to ensure optimal health of animals under your care by providing a clean environment and optimal nutrition for those animals. Keep records of animal care up to date and report on the health of the animals regularly. Work with the IACUC veterinarian to assure that any treatment protocols of sick or injured animals are carried out properly. Qualifications: Current ESU Student. Pay\nRate: $9.00 per hour Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. Some student employment positions will require students to pass an academic check as well. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
