    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8262?c=esu": {
      "title": "Theatre Scene Shop Production Assistant",
      "description": "Theatre Scene Shop Production Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Theatre Scene Shop Production Assistant United States | req8262 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Theatre Scene Shop Production Assistant Job\nSummary: This position will assist in the\norganization and maintenance\nof Theatre Scene Shop. Responsibilities: Organization and maintenance of Theatre Scene Shop. Help to construct and paint sets for University productions. Collaborate and oversee Play Production students working shop. Assist with other production departments as needed-- electric, props, costumes, and sound. Assist Production Designers as needed. Work may include activities like carpentry, scenic painting, hang and focus of lighting equipment, and building and organization of props. Qualifications: Strong problem-solving skills. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail to ensure procedures are followed accurately. Reliability\nis important as this is a full semester commitment. Working Hours: 2-6pm Monday, Wednesday,\nand Friday with occasional evenings and weekends as needed to produce the show.\nThis position will require 10-15 hrs. weekly. Pay\nRate: Starting\nat $10.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8255?c=esu": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Microbiology & Parasitology",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Microbiology & Parasitology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Microbiology & Parasitology United States | req8255 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of\nBiological Sciences offers a quality education with a breadth of courses and\nopportunities for students to gain laboratory and field experience. Students\nmay earn a B.S. in Biology, Biotechnology, Environmental Studies, Marine\nScience, or Medical Technology. Concentrations within the B.S. in Biology\ninclude pre-professional programs, such as the Pre-Physician Assistant\nconcentration, to prepare students for careers in the health professions and a\nbiology secondary education program leading to teacher certification. In\naddition, the department offers an M.S. in Biology. Our state-of-the-art\nfacilities include applied biotechnology labs and a cell culture lab,\nsupporting research across fields such as genetics, molecular biology,\nmicrobiology and biotechnology. Scholarly activities are supported by both\ninternal and external funding opportunities. The successful candidate should have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, a commitment to teaching and mentoring diverse student populations, and a strong interest in serving students, the department, the university, and the broader community in a collegial, multidisciplinary environment. This full-time faculty role is set to begin August of 2026. Responsibilities: Teaching responsibilities will include courses in Microbiology (both lecture and lab) and Parasitology. Depending on the departmental needs, additional teaching responsibilities may include Introductory Biology I and II, Immunology, and Mechanisms of Disease. The candidate will have the opportunity to develop upper-level courses in their area of expertise. The teaching course load is 24 contact hours per academic year. Coordinating our Medical Technology major and Laboratory Medicine concentration in the Biology major. Establishing and maintaining an active research program in their expertise. This program should actively involve undergraduate and graduate students. Contribute to the M.S. program in biology by teaching graduate-level courses, mentoring student research, and serving on graduate student committees. Serve on departmental and university-wide committees. Qualifications: Ph.D. in Microbiology or related field. Applicants with all but the dissertation (ABD) will be considered, provided that the doctoral degree is awarded by August 2026. College teaching experience is required, with a demonstrated ability to teach both lecture and lab courses in Microbiology. An active track record of scholarly work in the field of expertise. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience in both lecture and lab courses in Parasitology. A demonstrated ability to involve undergraduate or graduate students in research. Experience in undergraduate academic advising. Experience and strong dedication to working with a diverse student population. Ability to implement active learning techniques in teaching practices. What We Offer: Outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Family Tuition waivers: Every full-time employee will receive a full tuition waiver for all ESU courses for themselves, spouse/domestic partner, and children. Every full-time employee will receive 50% tuition waiver at all PASSHE universities for themselves, spouse/domestic partner, and children. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant: Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and are required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter of application, cover letter expressing interest in the role, professional references, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy including how students will be involved in your research, unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before the appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three professional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final selection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful interview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference letters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time of employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud that ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8239?c=esu": {
      "title": "University Center Ambassadors",
      "description": "University Center Ambassadors | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) University Center Ambassadors United States | req8239 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search University Center Ambassadors Be\npart of the New University Center Team! The\nDivision of Economic Development and Entrepreneurship is seeking motivated\nstudents to join our University Center Ambassador Team. This role will provide\nopportunities to build leadership, customer service, and event management\nskills while playing a key role in welcoming students, faculty, and community\nmembers to ESU’s new hub for campus life. Why\nYou’ll Love This Role Flexible scheduling to fit your classes and commitments. $15.00 per hour pay rate. Be the go-to resource for students, visitors, and event guests. Gain hands-on experience with events, operations, and leadership. Your\nRole as a University Center Ambassador Customer Service & Information - Be the welcoming face of ESU! You’ll greet visitors, answer questions, assist by phone, and help guests navigate events and services throughout the building. Building Operations - Help keep the center running smoothly by checking rooms, ensuring spaces are ready for events, and assisting with opening/closing procedures. Event Support - Organize campus events by setting up rooms, posting signage on bulleting boards, and making sure events follow university guidelines. Administrative Support - Build professional office skills with tasks like data entry, inventory tracking, and campus deliveries. Skills\n& Qualifications University Center Ambassadors are\ndependable, professional students who can represent ESU with excellence in a\nfast-paced, customer-focused environment. Ideal candidates will demonstrate: Strong Interpersonal & Communication Skills – Ability to provide courteous and professional assistance to students, staff, faculty and visitors. Organizational & Multitasking Ability – Capable of managing multiple priorities, maintaining orderly spaces, and ensuring events and schedules run smoothly. Technical Proficiency – Proficiency in using computer programs for data entry, scheduling, and administrative tasks with great attention to details. Dependability & Professionalism – Reliable attendance and a commitment to supporting building operations, including early morning, late night, and weekend shifts as needed. Work Hours The University Center will\noperate during the following hours: Monday – Friday: 7:30 a.m. – Midnight Saturday: Noon – Midnight Sunday: Noon – Midnight Weekend hours may be extended or adjusted to support major campus events such as athletic competitions, Homecoming, and other large-scale programs. Apply now or Learn More Interested\nstudents should contact the Office of Career and Workforce Development for more\ndetails about the application process and upcoming training opportunities. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8232?c=esu": {
      "title": "PSED Student Worker",
      "description": "PSED Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) PSED Student Worker United States | req8232 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The PSED Department is Searching for a Student Worker! Job Duties: General office support:-Assist secretary with general office duties including copy requests, scanning, assist walk-ins, mailings, etc. Front Desk Coverage-Greet students and visitors, manage the front desk, and provide a welcoming environment. Phone Management-Answer incoming call, take messages, and direct calls as appropriate. Errands-Run errands around campus, including picking up and dropping off print request. Project Assistance-Work on various projects as assigned by faculty and staff. Faculty Support-Assist faculty members with administrative tasks as needed. Qualifications: Student should be in academically good standing, good work ethics, able to follow directions, attention to detail, able to work independently as well as in a team work environment. Basic computer knowledge in Word, Excel, Power Point, Student\nPortal, D2L. Current ESU Student. Additional Information: Up to 20 hours per week subject to change. Hourly rate $9.00 Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8215?c=esu": {
      "title": "Faculty Assistant for COMM 126: Introduction to Mass Media",
      "description": "Faculty Assistant for COMM 126: Introduction to Mass Media | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Faculty Assistant for COMM 126: Introduction to Mass Media United States | req8215 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Faculty Assistant for CMST 126: Introduction to Mass Media The Program The Faculty Assistant (FA) program supports faculty who are teaching (three or four credit) classes of sixty (60) or more students (for classes of 120 or greater registered students, two FAs can be provided). The FA can assist faculty in any classroom activity deemed appropriate for 6 hours per week for 15 weeks at $8.00 per hour. Position Description Students participating in the East Stroudsburg University Large Class Assistant (FA) program are required to attend all classes for which they are providing support. FAs will work directly with professors who will outline their position responsibilities which may include: verifying class rosters, taking  attendance, arranging for technology services, and assisting with  maintaining and uploading course materials and information onto D2L. Additionally, FAs can assist with proctoring exams, scanning, copying, collating, distributing course materials, and updating bulletin boards. The Faculty Assistant may be assigned other duties as directed by the professor that are appropriate, but may not perform any functions as instructor of record, e.g., FAs are not to grade any course assignments. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8179?c=esu": {
      "title": "Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing",
      "description": "Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Maintenance Repairman 2 - Plumbing United States | req8179 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Maintenance Repairman 2, you will need to be comfortable repairing and maintaining the plumbing systems, HVAC equipment, piping systems, and associated equipment. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Facilities Operations Supervisor to complete routine tests to maintain steam lines. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your plumbing background with your excellent diagnostic skills all while timely executing requests to meet the needs of the ESU campus community . To be successful in this role, you must have strong attention to detail, problem-solving and technical skills. Your normal schedule will be Tuesday to Saturday 3:00 pm to 11:00 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Maintenance Repairman 2.  When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Employ established trade practices to install, repair, and do preventive maintenance on plumbing fixtures, HVAC systems, and other related equipment. Install, maintain, and repair valves, faucets, traps, sinks, and other sanitary fixtures. Install fixture supports and hangers. Maintain piping systems by opening clogged pipes and traps, repairing broken or leaking pipes, repairing steam lines, and repairing steam traps and regulators. Repair and or replace circulating pumps and backflow valves in the heating system. Bend, cut, and solder copper pipe and tubing; cut, ream, and thread steel pipe; cut and glue plastic pipe. Changes HVAC filters and maintains HVAC equipment and controls. Repair and replace electrical motors, controllers, switchboard panels, lights, power circuits, and electrical generators. Locate and correct power failures and short circuits, install open and concealed wiring and lighting fixtures. Install temporary wiring for special events that are held at various locations on campus. Maintain working knowledge of the use of the standard tools, equipment, and testing devices of the electrical trade. Operate trade equipment such as drills, hammers, testing equipment, hand tools, scaffolding, bench grinder, right angle grinder saline saw, saw, cherry picker/manlift. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Four years of experience in the plumbing and electrical trade, or completion of an approved apprenticeship; or any equivalent combination of experience and training. Able to think critically and apply critical thinking skills to solve problems independently. Able to quickly pivot between work tasks when unplanned events occur that need immediate attention. Valid PA Driver’s License. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $41,506 annually Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7931?c=esu": {
      "title": "25-28 CY Physical Education Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "25-28 CY Physical Education Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 25-28 CY Physical Education Adjunct Pool United States | req7931 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Physical Education offers two programs at the undergraduate level; teacher certification and a\nnon-teacher certification to prepare the contemporary professional. The program is Nationally Accredited, and\nall faculty are highly engaged within the discipline and have active research\nagendas in which to include students. ESU's Department of Physical Education offers a BS in Physical Education with a dual major in Physical Education and\nHealth Education to enhance the professional preparation of the students. Qualifications: Minimum of a MS in\nPhysical Education. Professional teaching experience in public schools. Valid driver's license Ability to supervise student teachers. What We Offer If eligible, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through\nthe ESU Job Portal and are required to attach the following to the online\napplication:  a letter of application, curriculum vitae, statement of\nteaching philosophy, unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts\n(official transcripts required before the appointment), and contact information\nincluding e-mail addresses for three professional references. Upload all\ndocuments to the online application. Final selection will be based on a review\nof the candidate’s vita and a successful interview (If conducted by the search\ncommittee). Only confidential reference letters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must\nprovide proof of eligibility to work in the United States and official\ntranscripts at the time of employment. Employment Eligiblity & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7927?c=esu": {
      "title": "Temporary Research Technician",
      "description": "Temporary Research Technician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temporary Research Technician United States | req7927 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Temporary Research Technician, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable conducting advanced scientific experimentation to evaluate various environmental and biological sample types. You will be an active member of the Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife Genetics Institute team and will work closely with the Director to skillfully perform test procedures in search of pathogens from specimens. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your biology or veterinary background and professional laboratory experience all while utilizing various apparatuses to execute DNA/RNA procedures or polymerase chain reactions. To be successful in this role the applicant must be eager to learn a breadth of techniques, strong critical thinking and communication skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule to work evenings or weekends from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Temporary Research Technician. This role requires up to 10% travel. This is a temporary full time grant funded role until 6/30/2025 contingent upon continued grant renewal. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Maintaining successful completion of proficiency testing in aseptic techniques, DNA/RNA extractions, and PCR. Performs laboratory testing using scientific techniques, such as DNA/RNA extractions, and polymerase chain reaction (PCR) to determine the presence, or absence of bacterial, protozoa, fungi, viruses, or other pathogenic microorganisms. Performs laboratory testing using scientific techniques such as genotyping, and genetic sequencing to evaluate genotypes, strain, and haplotype differences of pathogens or wildlife populations. Maintains data using electronic recording and documentation of sample processing based on approved standards of practice. Conducts required quality assurance and quality control procedures to ensure reagents, media, apparatus, and processes meet required performance standards. Assists with generating scientific protocols to be used in research conducted within the laboratory and assist Research Assistant with projects on tick-borne illnesses or population genetics. Identify various ticks to species and life stages and ability to use dichotomous keys to identify unknown specimens. Maintains, cleans, and calibrates all scientific equipment based on manufacturers and laboratory standards of practice. Updates and maintains current standards of practice and inventory logs and processes. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Associates degree in Veterinary Laboratory Technology (VLT) or Medical Laboratory Technician (MLT) and one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory. Or Two years of college which includes six (6) credits in biology, three (3) credits in chemistry, and three (3) credits in microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, histology or biostatistics and one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory. Or An equivalent combination of experience and training which included one (1) year of technical laboratory experience in a biomedical research or development, clinical pathology or diagnostic laboratory, and six (6) college credits in biology, three (3) college credits in chemistry, and three (3) college credits in microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, histology or biostatistics. One year of experience work in a research laboratory or one-year technical laboratory experience or any equivalent combination of experience and training. A Bachelor’s degree of Science in Microbiology, Biology, Biotechnology, or a related field with a minimum of 20 credit hours in Genetics, Molecular Biology, Biotechnology, Microbiology, Cellular Biology, and Biochemistry preferred. Minimum of 1-year experience working in a molecular, biotechnology or similar laboratory preferred. One-year experience with sample handling, DNA extractions, and Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is preferred. One-year experience identifying ticks and knowledge on ticks and tick-borne diseases in Pennsylvania is preferred. Strong communication skills to efficiently with lead laboratory staff on experimentations and laboratory processes. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits\n     package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement\n     contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $1,795.50 biweekly Living\n     by the Warrior Code: Accountable\n      for One's Actions Committed\n      to Self-Growth Willing\n      to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive,\n      Honest, and Loyal Respectful\n      of the Environment and Community Dedicated\n      to Empowering Others \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write\nEnglish. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a\nthorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse,\nand employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here:\nhttps://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7886?c=esu": {
      "title": "Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life",
      "description": "Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life United States | req7886 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable leading developments centered around student success & retention to create a flourishing Fraternity & Sorority Life (FSL) community. You will be an active member of the Campus Life and Inclusive Excellence team and will work closely with the Dean of Student Life to build and implement strategic plans to support the needs of the FSL community. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your student affairs background, and your direct experience working with Fraternities & Sororities all while developing various comprehensive trainings to assist new and current FSL members. To be successful in this role, you must possess working knowledge of organizational program development, have previous professional experience in fraternity and or sorority life, and excellent communication skills. Your normal schedule will be Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Director of Fraternity and Sorority Life. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Leadership & Administration Provide strategic leadership and vision for fraternity and sorority life, including short and long-range planning, program development, and community building. Develop and implement a comprehensive training and development program for FSL members, including a hazing awareness and prevention plan which fosters a culture of safety and respect. Oversee the departmental budget, ensuring fiscal responsibility and strategic allocation of resources. Student Support Collaborate with all Councils to develop a comprehensive recruitment plan for all chapters that includes working with the recruitment chair, the Release Figure Methodology (RFM) specialist and using software platforms such as Omega Fi, etc. Implement an updated accreditation process that reflects the strategic plan for the FSL program and is aligned with standards for student success and chapter development. Works directly with chapter leadership to track and review new member education programs which include maintaining appropriate paperwork regarding chapter rosters, new member paperwork, and all appropriate policies. Community Engagement and Partnerships Coordinate with multiple administrative units to ensure that standards, reporting, training, assessment, and advising among all fraternities and sororities are consistent and meet best practices and to ensure cooperative programming/involvement for all Greek-letter organizations. Build and sustain relationships with chapter advisors that promote development and growth of all organizations. Assist in promoting the core values of all council\norganizations, the achievement of goals and development of new and existing\nmembers. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Master’s degree in higher education administration, student affairs, counseling or another related field. Minimum of three years of professional experience in fraternity and/or sorority life. Demonstrated understanding of student development theory in practice. Comprehensive knowledge of the governing bodies which set the standards for fraternities and sororities. Demonstrated commitment to understanding and working with a diverse student population. Working experience in student success and retention initiatives, including but limited to risk management. Demonstrated proficiency in assessment, organizational program development, and community engagement. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $61,966 annually Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7833?c=esu": {
      "title": "Director of the Office of Sponsored Research and Grants",
      "description": "Director of the Office of Sponsored Research and Grants | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of the Office of Sponsored Research and Grants United States | req7833 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Director you will need to think creatively and be comfortable overseeing the departments administration, coordination, and compliance of external funding for research and academic projects. You will be an active member of the Academic Affairs team and will work closely with the Provost to further boost ESU’s reputation as a driving force in research.  This role will pioneer the streamlining of the grants application process, offering strategic guidance to the campus community, and ensuring financial compliance throughout the lifecycle of sponsored research. The Director will also lead a dynamic team of professionals to maximize research funding opportunities while adhering federal, state and institutional policies. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your research administration background and grant management experience all while cultivating a vibrant community conducive to cutting-edge research. To be successful in this role the applicant must possess progressive supervisory experience, a strong working knowledge of relevant ordinances for grants & research projects, and proven leadership skills. Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm, but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Director of the Office of Sponsored Research and Grants. There is up to 10% travel for the role. When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Leadership & Strategy: Provide strategic direction\nfor and management of the Office of Sponsored Research and Grants, ensuring\nalignment with the institution's mission, goals, and research priorities. Serve as the primary\nliaison between the institution and external funding agencies, including\nfederal, state, and private sector sponsors. Grants & Proposal Management: Oversee the preparation,\nreview, and submission of grant proposals to federal, state, and private\nfunding organizations ensuring compliance with sponsor guidelines,\ninstitutional policies, and federal regulations. Coordinate with principal\ninvestigators to ensure successful grant applications and facilitate the\npreparation of research proposals that meet sponsor guidelines. Compliance & Oversight: Ensure\n     adherence to federal, state, institutional, and sponsor-specific\n     regulations regarding research grants, contracts, and financial\n     management, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200), IRB protocols, and\n     export control regulations. Serve\n     as the primary point of contact for external agencies regarding sponsored\n     research compliance issues. Budget & Resource Management: Coordinate\n     with appropriate offices the preparation of budgets for grant proposals, ensuring\n     that budgeted research expenses remain within approved parameters. Work\n     with departmental and central administration staff to track and report on\n     grant funds utilization. Outreach & Education: Develop and deliver\neducational programs, workshops, and seminars for faculty and staff to improve\nknowledge and skills in securing and managing sponsored research. Stay current on trends,\nchanges in funding agency priorities, and new research grant regulations to\ninform best practices. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Master's degree (Ph.D. or equivalent\npreferred) in a related field such as Research Administration, Business\nAdministration, or a field closely aligned with the institution’s research\npriorities. A minimum of 7-10 years of\nexperience in research administration, including significant experience with\ngrants management, budgeting, and compliance. At least 3 years of\nsupervisory experience, with a demonstrated ability to lead and manage teams\neffectively. Familiarity with federal\nfunding agencies (e.g., NIH, NSF, DOE) and private funding sources. Strong understanding of the\npolicies, regulations, and procedures governing sponsored research in higher\neducation. Proficient in grants\nmanagement software, project management tools, and Microsoft Office Suite\n(Excel, Word, PowerPoint). Excellent communication\nskills, both written and verbal, with the ability to articulate complex\nconcepts to diverse audiences. Exceptional organizational,\nproblem-solving, and time management skills. Ability to work\ncollaboratively across departments, with faculty, administrators, and external\npartners. High level of integrity,\nattention to detail, and commitment to ethical standards in research and\nfinancial management. Valid Drivers License. Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: Based on Experience Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7381?c=esu": {
      "title": "Carpenter 1",
      "description": "Carpenter 1 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Carpenter 1 United States | req7381 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search As the Carpenter 1, you will need to think creatively and be comfortable performing skilled work in several trades in carpentry. You will be an active member of the Facilities Management team and will work closely with the Building Maintenance Foreman to remove damaged materials and perform full demolition of existing structures. You will thrive in this role if you like combining your carpentry experience and knowledge of electrical assignments all while utilizing various different tools to maintain ESU facilities. To be successful in this role, you must be detail-oriented , have a strong work ethic and hi gh standards to perform quality independent work . Your normal hours will be Monday to Friday 7:30 AM – 3:30 PM , but you may have to flex your schedule from time to time based on the needs of the business to be a true Carpen ter 1 . When our team shows up for work, they are energized and motivated to succeed - all while being the most crucial piece to keeping the ESU operations humming. What Will I Do At ESU? (AKA Essential Duties) Operate and use all necessary machinery, tools, and equipment including but not limited to bench saw and joiners, band saw, overhead saw, belt sander, electric drill press, electric grinder, key-making machine, skill saw, saber saw, electric planers, router, and other equipment incidental to the trade. Responsible for r epair ing , replac ing , and install ing new screening doors (wood and metal) and windows. Repair wood and tile flooring and assist in laying new concrete. Repair and replace locks and cylinders and make new keys. Construct or repair tables, chairs, bleachers, steps, and athletic equipment. Repair and install tracks for draperies and blinds. Construct classrooms and offices, install blackboards, make, and repair bulletin boards, and construct and install shelving. Complete all necessary wood and drywall construction. Repair roof(s) with available materials including shingles and slate. Read and interpret construction blueprints and drawings. What We're Looking For (AKA Qualifications) Three years of experience in the construction, installation, repair, restoration, or maintenance of structures and articles made from wood, composite, and wood substitute materials or an equivalent combination of experience and training. 1-year of Commercial Construction experience preferred Valid C Driver’s License. Ability to lift, carry, push and pull 50lb minimum, and extensive hand coordination movement required . Ability to work in inclement weather. Comprehension of written and oral communication. Knowledge of skilled carpentry and electrical assignments in accordance with the standard practice of the trade. Basic computer skills, web browser for email and compliance training. Ability to work independently and use judgment when performing work tasks related to skillset. Experience with Word, Excel, Teams required . Able to read, write, and comprehend English; able to follow verbal instructions. What We Offer Outstanding benefits package including benefits such as medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Salary: $41,506 annually Living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Positive, Honest, and Loyal Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others \"Employment Eligibility & University Commitment\" Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7271?c=esu": {
      "title": "24-27 CY English Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "24-27 CY English Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 24-27 CY English Adjunct Pool United States | req7271 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The English Department\nis seeking to add to the existing Adjunct Faculty pool, which we established in\nFall 2023. We need faculty to teach ENGL 101 and ENGL 103 and potentially\nintroductory courses in literature (e.g. ENGL 162) and/or business writing (e.g.\nENGL 205) in the future. To be successful in\nthis position, the candidate will be an effective\nteacher and mentor for students and an active member of the department.\nApplications on-hand will be used to fill vacancies as needed. Qualifications: A master’s degree in English or related field is required. Applicant must have relevant teaching experience in college composition and college-level writing courses. Must be able to speak, read, write, and comprehend English; able to create clear verbal and written messages. Preferred: Experience working with diverse student populations, a terminal degree in English or related field (either a Ph.D. or M.F.A), experience teaching introductory literature courses, and experience in teaching distance education are preferred. What We Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills.\nEmployment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough\nbackground check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and\nemployment/degree verifications. We are proud that ESU is an equal-opportunity\nemployer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7074?c=esu": {
