    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/7004?c=esu": {
      "title": "24 - 27 CY History Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "24 - 27 CY History Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 24 - 27 CY History Adjunct Pool United States | req7004 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of History and Geography at East Stroudsburg\nUniversity is establishing a three-year, temporary faculty teaching pool.\nCandidates must be able to teach one or more of the following: US History to\n1877, US History since 1877, World History to 1500 and World History since 1800. The successful candidate will be an\nactive member of the department and will work to develop and mentor students.\n  Applications on hand will be used to fill vacancies as needed. ESU's History and Geography Department offers several\nprograms of study that lead to a Bachelor of Arts degree.  The program offers a comprehensive foundation of\ncourses and an opportunity for students to select elective courses within\nspecific areas of History to prepare students to excel in their career\nand life. Qualifications M.A. in History, College Teaching Experience, Experience Teaching in a Diverse Environment What\nWe Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6995?c=esu": {
      "title": "24-27 CY Exercise Science Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "24-27 CY Exercise Science Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 24-27 CY Exercise Science Adjunct Pool United States | req6995 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Exercise Science offers a breadth of degrees and\ncredentials to prepare the contemporary professional.  State-of-the-art laboratories and strong\ncommunity clinical partners provide students with practical experience\nnecessary to compete in the competitive job market and admission into\nprofessional schools (DPT, OT, PA). All faculty are highly engaged within the\ndiscipline and have active research agendas in which to include students. ESU's Department of Exercise Science offers a BS in Exercise\nScience, MS in Clinical Exercise Physiology, MS in Exercise Science, and\nDoctorate of Health Sciences. In addition, a Nutrition Certificate, Sport\nPerformance Coaching Certificate and Health Coaching Minor are available to\nenhance the professional preparation of the students. Qualifications MUST HAVE a minimum of a MS in Exercise Science or related discipline, teaching experience in laboratory settings (human performance and biomechanics), and ability to sit for one of the NCCA-accredited credentials within the discipline. What We Offer--- If eligible, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud that ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6734?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Theater Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "26-29 CY Theater Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 26-29 CY Theater Adjunct Pool United States | req6734 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Theatre at East Stroudsburg University is establishing a temporary faculty\nteaching pool. Candidates must be able to teach Introduction to Theatre\ncourses. The successful candidate will be an active member of the department\nand will work to develop and mentor students.  Applications on-hand will\nbe used to fill vacancies as needed. ESU's Theatre Department offers several programs of study that\nlead to a Bachelor of Theatre degree. \nThe program offers a comprehensive foundation of courses and an opportunity for\nstudents to select elective courses within specific areas of theatre to prepare\nstudents to excel in their career and life. Qualifications Ph.D. or Master of Fine Arts in Theatre or a related field University-level teaching experience preferred What\nWe Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
