    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6528?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Philosophy & Religious Studies Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "26-29 CY Philosophy & Religious Studies Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 26-29 CY Philosophy & Religious Studies Adjunct Pool United States | req6528 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The department offers coursework leading to a minor or a major in\nPhilosophy. The major offers three different concentrations: Leadership in\nDiverse Communities, Knowledge and Critical Reasoning, and Religion and Global\nThought. ESU's Philosophy majors boast an excellent record of hiring and\ngraduate study acceptances. Located\nin the beautiful Pocono Mountains of Pennsylvania, ESU’s proximity to New York\nCity and Philadelphia provides students with convenient access to internships,\ncareers and social activities. Just minutes from campus are the country’s\nlargest water parks, scenic Delaware Water Gap Recreation Area, Appalachian\nTrail, and other opportunities for recreational fun. Qualifications A Masters degree in a relevant field is required; a doctorate is preferred. Must have significant teaching experience in a higher ed setting with a diverse student population. What We Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union and APSCUF faculty union. Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to\nApplicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
