    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6376?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Reading Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "26-29 CY Reading Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 26-29 CY Reading Adjunct Pool United States | req6376 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Reading at East Stroudsburg University\nis establishing a temporary faculty teaching pool. Candidates must be\nable to teach one or more of the following: REED 314: Foundations of Reading for the Developing Child REED 315: Teaching Reading to Students with Disabilities REED 340: Teaching Reading to Middle-Level Students REED 350: Teaching Reading to Diverse Learners (Secondary Level) The successful candidate will be an\nactive member of the department and will work to develop and mentor students. Applications on-hand will be used to fill vacancies as needed. ESU's Reading Department\noffers a master's degree, reading specialist certification, and serves several\nundergraduate programs. Qualifications Minimum degree of Master’s in Reading Education Experience in teaching Reading in the PK-12 setting Experience in teaching online What\nWe Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6374?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Sociology, Social Work & Criminal Justice Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "26-29 CY Sociology, Social Work & Criminal Justice Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 26-29 CY Sociology, Social Work & Criminal Justice Adjunct Pool United States | req6374 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Sociology,\nSocial Work & Criminal Justice at East Stroudsburg University is\nestablishing a three-year, temporary faculty teaching pool. All candidates must\nbe able to teach the introductory, theory and practice courses within their\nacademic disciplines. Candidates for\nsociology must also be able to teach general education course offerings. Candidates for social work must have an\nMSW degree with at least 2 years post-graduate practice experience and be a\nlicensed social work practitioner. It\nis also expected that candidates for criminal justice have experience working\nin the criminal justice field. Applications\non-hand will be used to fill vacancies as needed. Distance learning and/or\noff-campus teaching opportunities may be possible. ESU's Department of Sociology,\nSocial Work and Criminal Justice offers several programs of study that lead to a Bachelor’s degree. Students can complete the Bachelor of Arts Program in Sociology, the CSWE\nAccredited Bachelor of Science in Social Work (BSSW) Program or the Bachelor of\nScience in Criminal Justice Program. Each\nprogram prepares students to excel in their chosen field of study Qualifications Competency to teach courses in sociology or social work or criminal justice Master’s Degree in Sociology, Social Work, Criminal Justice/Criminology and/or a related field is required. A Ph.D. Degree in Sociology, Social Work or Criminal Justice/Criminology is preferred. Candidate should demonstrate teaching excellence in areas of competence. Candidates for social work positions must have an MSW degree with at least 2 years post-graduate practice experience and be a licensed social work practitioner. Candidates for criminal justice positions should have work experience in the criminal justice field. Experience working with diverse populations preferred. Final selection will be based on excellence in scholastic achievement, a review of the candidate’s curriculum vitae and a successful interview. What We Offer If qualified, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid holiday leave. Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at\nleast 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is\ncontingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information\non President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6373?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Mathematics Adjunct Pool",
