    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/6313?c=esu": {
      "title": "26-29 CY Biological Sciences Adjunct Pool",
      "description": "26-29 CY Biological Sciences Adjunct Pool | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) 26-29 CY Biological Sciences Adjunct Pool United States | req6313 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search The Department of Biological Sciences at East Stroudsburg\nUniversity is establishing a three-year temporary faculty teaching pool. Applications for\ntemporary vacancies are accepted on an on-going basis. Applications on-hand will be used to fill\nvacancies as needed. Qualifications Applicant\nmust be competent to teach courses in Introductory Biology; Human Anatomy and\nPhysiology; and/or Microbiology (both lecture and laboratory). A Masters in\nBiological Sciences and/or a related field is required. Candidate should demonstrate\nteaching excellence in areas of competence. Distance learning and/or off-campus\nteaching opportunities may be possible. Experience working with diverse\npopulations preferred. A Ph.D. degree in Biological Sciences is preferred. What We Offer--- If eligible, outstanding benefits package including medical from date of hire, retirement contributions, employee wellness program, and paid leave Optional membership to PSECU Credit Union Community commitment to living by the Warrior Code: Accountable for One's Actions Positive, Honest, and Loyal Committed to Self-Growth Willing to Sacrifice for the Greater Good Respectful of the Environment and Community Dedicated to Empowering Others Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must apply through the ESU Job Portal and\nare required to attach the following to the online application:  a letter\nof application, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial\nundergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts required before\nthe appointment), and contact information including e-mail addresses for three\nprofessional references. Upload all documents to the online application. Final\nselection will be based on a review of the candidate’s vita and a successful\ninterview (If conducted by the search committee). Only confidential reference\nletters are accepted at askhr@esu.edu. All candidates must provide proof of\neligibility to work in the United States and official transcripts at the time\nof employment. Employment Eligibility & University Committment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with\nESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check\nthat includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree\nverifications. We are proud that ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more\ninformation on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8261?c=esu": {
      "title": "General Office Assistant Art+Media+Design",
      "description": "General Office Assistant Art+Media+Design | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) General Office Assistant Art+Media+Design United States | req8261 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 11/5/2025 Back to Search The Art+Media+Design & Theater Departments are searching for a motivated students to serve as the General Office Assistant. Job Summary: An experienced office assistant for the Fine Arts Building that will help greet students, staff and faculty in the Fine Arts Office. Assistants will help to answer the phone, cover the front desk and help with daily tasks like copying, data entry and filing. Assistants will work a set schedule throughout the semester. Answering telephones Piano Maintenance Making photocopies & Sorting mail Helping students & assisting faculty members with various tasks/duties Occasional typing / computer work. Assisting the Administrative Assistant and Department Chair with various office tasks. Qualifications: Excellent customer service skills. General knowledge of computers. Strong problem-solving skills. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Communication skills. Strong attention to detail. Excellent organizational skills a must. Reliability as this is a full semester commitment. Additional Information: $12 hourly Up to 20 hours per week. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and be able to read and write English. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8260?c=esu": {
      "title": "Student Model",
      "description": "Student Model | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Student Model United States | req8260 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 11/5/2025 Back to Search East Stroudsburg University’s Department of Art + Media + Design are searching for Student Models Job Duties: The student model will pose for\nthe art class under the direction of the professor. Models will be required to hold\nvarious poses, including dynamic and static positions, for specified durations\nto facilitate the drawing, painting, or sculpting process for students. Qualifications: Current ESU student. Reliable as this is a semester long commitment Ability to hold poses for extended periods. Additional Information: Hourly rate of pay $15. Up to 20 hours per week. Eligible under work study program. Employment Eligibility & University Commitment Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8828?c=esu": {
      "title": "Admissions Front Desk Student Worker",
      "description": "Admissions Front Desk Student Worker | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Admissions Front Desk Student Worker United States | req8828 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Admissions Front Desk Student Worker Position Summary: Admissions Front Desk Workers are responsible for assisting daily\noperations of the Admissions Office. This includes assisting the front of\nhouse operations, and are expected to assist with walk-ins, phone calls, basic\nprocessing tasks, data entry, and supporting the Assistant Directors with daily\ntasks. Responsibilities: Assist with outbound calls, answer incoming calls, screen telephone calls, assist with walk-ins. Data entry and filing. Process incoming mail. Occasional day/weekend events. Complete occasional campus wide errands. Assist with the organization and upkeep of the office. Assist with office supply inventory. Assist with advising students and their families on necessary steps for completing admissions forms, registering for events, and logging into their portals. Assist the Admissions Office with processing admissions forms for potential students. Interacting with students via email and phone, addressing any questions or concerns. Must maintain confidentiality working with highly sensitive information. Qualifications: Be enrolled at ESU as a full-time student. Maintain a 2.5 cumulative and semester GPA. Be in good academic and judicial standing. Basic computer skills and knowledge. Ability to professionally interact with customers in the role at all times. Customer service, communication and phone skills. Knowledge of campus, events, offices, and offerings. Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment. Must be able to work at least 10 hours a week. Understanding of the Family Educational Rights to Privacy ACT (FERPA). Compensation: $12 per hour Employment Eligibility & University Commitment: Must be at least 18 years old and have English literacy skills. Employment with ESU is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and employment/degree verifications. We are proud ESU is an equal-opportunity employer. For more information on President Long's 10-point plan, click here: https://www.esu.edu/president/10-action-plan.cfm Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8834?c=esu": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Worker - Wildlife Field Technician - Winter 2026",
      "description": "Graduate Student Worker - Wildlife Field Technician - Winter 2026 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Graduate Student Worker - Wildlife Field Technician - Winter 2026 United States | req8834 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Graduate Student Wildlife\nField Technician (Graduate Student Worker) at the Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife\nGenetics Institute Job Description: The Dr. Jane Huffman Wildlife Genetics Institute is seeking\na Graduate Student Wildlife Field Technician in our vector borne disease\nlaboratory, collecting and testing ticks for disease agents. This is a unique\nopportunity to support research on vector borne disease.The candidate will conduct field work collecting ticks and\nother reservoir host for analysis. Following collections, the candidate will\nconduct DNA extractions and real-time PCR. Other duties will include importing\nscientific data and assisting with other field-related duties. The Graduate\nStudent Lab Technician also will need to clean and calibrate equipment, measure\ncompounds, and prepare solutions for use. Responsibilities: Responsible adherence to laboratory and field safety procedures Collecting and identifying ticks Carrying out scientific research using molecular techniques, such as DNA/RNA extractions, polymerase chain reaction (PCR) and gel electrophoresis Inputting data into computer programs and utilizing statistical software for analysis Analyzing and interpreting data Preparing a manuscript for submission to a peer-reviewed journal Required Skills: A current Graduate student with a minimum of 9 credit hours in Genetics, Molecular Biology, Biotechnology and Microbiology. Experience in DNA extraction, Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR), Tick identification and DNA sequencing is preferred. Successful candidates will be self-motivated, organized, independent, and eager to learn a breadth of techniques. Occasional evening and/or weekend work will be required. Please submit updated transcripts, resume and cover letter\nto complete the application process. Salary = $15.00/hour 40 hours/week Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here:http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://ESU.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/6/home/requisition/8833?c=esu": {
      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Residential Life & Housing Spring - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Residential Life & Housing Spring - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Residential Life & Housing Spring - 2027 United States | req8833 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search GRADUATE\nASSISTANT FOR RESIDENTIAL LIFE AND HOUSING MANAGEMENT/\nSUPERVISION: Reports to the Assistant Director of Residential Life and Housing (or designated professional within Residential Life and Housing). COMPENSATION: Graduate School Tuition Waiver (Does not include fees) Full Housing Waiver (due to residential and campus responsibilities throughout the academic year) $8.34 Hourly Rate of Pay WORK HOURS\nPER WEEK: 20 hours per week during the Academic Semester. Hours are required between 8 a.m. and 4:30 p.m. Additional Hours required during move-in, move-out, and training periods of the academic year. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's Degree in chosen field(s) of study. Accepted and enrolled at East Stroudsburg University as a Graduate Student Remain in good academic standing by maintaining a minimum overall Grade Point Average (GPA) of 3.0 during the period of employment. Failure to maintain the minimum GPA may result in loss of employment or other disciplinary action. GA must stay in good conduct standing with The University during employment. BACKGROUND\nCHECK REQUIREMENTS: Employment with ESU as a Graduate Assistant is contingent on the selected candidate passing a thorough background check that includes: FBI fingerprinting, PA Child Abuse, and past employment. ACADEMIC YEAR\nEMPLOYMENT DATES: SPRING 2027 -The Graduate\nAssistant will move-in on Monday, January 4, 2027.  Training will begin on Tuesday, January 5,\n2027. The Spring 2027 Employment date will end on May 14, 2027, unless indicated by supervisor of an earlier date. The Graduate Assistant will hold no other commitments through May 14, 2027, without the written approval and permission of their supervisor. **Note: Start Date for Spring 2027 is tentative and will be finalized by\nNovember 30th, 2026. IMPORTANT DATES FOR REFERENCE-SPRING 2027: January 17, 2027 - Residence Halls Open for Spring 2027 Semester. January 19, 2027- First Day of Spring 2027 classes March 6, 2027 - Residence Halls Close at 12 p.m./Noon for Spring Break. Graduate Assistants are required to stay until Hall Closings tasks are completed. March 14, 2027 - Residence Halls Open at 12:00 p.m./Noon. Graduate Assistants and those scheduled to work are required to return by 12:00 p.m./ Noon May 8, 2027 - Residence Halls Close for the Spring 2027 Semester at 12 p.m./Noon RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE: Oversee residential communities and lead Resident Advisor (RA) staff teams assigned for the 26-27 academic year. Select, train, lead, and evaluate hall staff, which will include Resident Advisors and Desk Assistants. Provide leadership coaching for the Resident Hall Council of the building in organizing and implementing events for students Plan and facilitate weekly student RA staff meetings to coordinate initiatives, share information and provide ongoing training and development Provide direction and accountability to student staff for the enforcement and proper documentation of Housing and Residence Life policies Create opportunities for team building, interaction, and cooperation for Residential Life team members (residence hall staff and leadership team) Meet regularly with student staff members to discuss community issues, resident concerns, and monitor progress of the staff member Meet regularly with leadership team members to provide ongoing training, discuss upcoming events, provide direction and guidance, and evaluate activities. Complete assigned organizational projects and committee work Perform administrative tasks in accordance with established Housing and Residence Life procedures and deadlines Utilize The Housing Director (THD) to assist with occupancy management and front desk operations Manage internal residence hall budget Address and monitor facility concerns, maintenance, repairs, and cleanliness Provide and promote educational opportunities focusing on awareness and appreciation of cultural differences and building an inclusive and respectful community Promote and support the mission and vision of East Stroudsburg University, the Campus Life and Inclusive Excellence Division, and Housing and Residence Life Support activities planned and implemented by the hall's student staff and Leadership Team promote an environment conducive to academic success, development, and learning Be available to assist in all openings and all closings of their assigned residence hall Build in good working relationship with student staff and Pro Staff. Serve as a resource and referral person for university operations and the functions of the various University administrative offices. Actively and regularly communicate with supervisor and other staff members using multiple means (electronic and in person) as defined by supervisor. Recognize and fulfill responsibilities with evacuation drills and other emergency situations. Maintain clear communications and positive working relationships with ALL University staff members. Assist in identifying and reporting housekeeping, maintenance, and safety problems. Respect individual privacy and the confidential nature of information about individual students. Maintain regular office hours and be available to assist during special nights and weekends (opening, closing, etc.). Intentionally and actively practice the Way of the Warrior tenants. Remain in good academic standing by maintaining a minimum overall Grade Point Average (GPA) of 3.0 during the period of employment.Failure to maintain the minimum GPA may result in loss of employment or other disciplinary action. GA’s must stay in good conduct standing with The University during employment. Comply with and enforce all Federal, State and Local Laws, as well as all University regulations. Other duties as assigned. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
