      "title": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Health Studies/MPH Program Spring - 2027",
      "description": "(GA) Graduate Assistant - Health Studies/MPH Program Spring - 2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) (GA) Graduate Assistant - Health Studies/MPH Program Spring - 2027 United States | req8831 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/21/2026 Back to Search Type of Position: Graduate Assistant with the Health Studies department working 10 hours per week/150 hours per semester. Pay Rate: $8.34 per hour Job Summary: Assists public health program\ndirector in tracking accreditation-mandated performance measures for upcoming\nreaccreditation review inclusive of alumni performance tracking, community\npartner interaction, and completion of data tracking forms.  Additionally, the GA may be asked to perform any\ncombination of following duties: Responsibilities: Assist in developing teaching materials, such as syllabi's and visual aids. Assist in laboratory or field research. Assist in library searches. Assist in maintaining database of active students and alumni. Assist faculty member with research, program management, and service. Maintaining database of field-based placement sites. Documenting accreditation-based performance measures. Specific tasks will be explained to assistant by faculty supervisor at time of appointment. Overseeing the public health program’s social media accounts. Required Qualifications: Graduate Student in the\nHealth Studies Department. Preferred Qualifications: Proficient with basic\ncomputer software, student in good academic standing, experience with marketing\nand management of social media platforms. Annual Clery Crime and Fire statistics report: East Stroudsburg University (ESU) has made a commitment to ensure the safety of its students, employees and visitors. The annual security and fire safety compliance document is available on the ESU website here: http://www4.esu.edu/about/offices/police/documents/pdf/annual_publication.pdf If you would like to receive a paper copy of the “East Stroudsburg University Police Annual Clery Crime and Fire Statistics Publication” which contains this information, you can request that a copy be mailed to you by calling (570) 422-3064. The website and booklet contain information regarding campus security and personal safety including topics such as: crime prevention, fire safety, university police law enforcement authority, crime reporting policies, disciplinary procedures and other matters of importance related to security and safety on campus. They also contain information about crime statistics for the three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by ESU; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from the campus. About ESU: East Stroudsburg University of Pennsylvania (ESU) is located in Northeastern Pennsylvania in the scenic Pocono Mountains and adjacent to the Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area. Founded in 1893, ESU is one of 14 university members of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education and has a current enrollment of 6,742. The University offers 55 undergraduate degree programs and 22 graduate degree programs and one doctoral program, the university is poised for continued growth. The surrounding community offers options for suburban, small city, or country living all within a less than two-hour drive to both New York City and Philadelphia. Apply Now Share Save Job"
